1
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:07,549
<i>( Thunder crashes)</i>

2
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:10,469
<i>(swing music playing)</i>

3
00:00:12,637 --> 00:00:14,139
( Rain falling )

4
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,672
( Music ceases )

5
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,009
BILLY: Whoa!

6
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:44,187
STEPHANIE:
All the food's gonna go bad.

7
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,108
Yeah, I drew up a list.

8
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:51,444
I'll hit the store
before it gets all bought out.

9
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,156
Fuck.

10
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:57,701
- Can you save it?
- No. No way.

11
00:01:57,784 --> 00:02:00,370
No, I gotta start over from scratch.

12
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:02,706
I'll call the studio
when the phones get back up,

13
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,416
see if they can extend my deadline.

14
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,294
STEPHANIE:
What choice do they have?

15
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,879
( David sighs heavily )

16
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:10,964
You kiddin'?

17
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:13,842
They could whip up some bad
Photoshop poster in an afternoon.

18
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:16,177
They do it all the time.
Two big heads.

19
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:18,179
I should have brought it downstairs
with me last night.

20
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:19,889
Just stupid, I guess.

21
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,975
Well, sweetie,
you couldn't exactly know

22
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:23,977
that a tree was gonna come flying
through the window.

23
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,478
Yeah, I'll hit the hardware store too,

24
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,105
get some plastic sheeting
and duct tape

25
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:29,357
and seal this up
before it gets dark, you know.

26
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:31,026
Order in some new glass.

27
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,820
Oh, you know what?
That was your--

28
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:36,448
That was your grandfather's tree,
the one he planted.

29
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:39,242
- Ohh.
- Used to play in that tree.

30
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:40,493
It's just stuff, though.

31
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:43,038
You know, we're safe.
That's all that counts.

32
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,205
Yeah.

33
00:02:44,289 --> 00:02:45,874
Mom, Dad, you gotta come see!

34
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,709
Hey, Billy, take it easy, all right?

35
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:49,502
I really don't want you running
all over the place.

36
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:50,670
But you gotta come look.

37
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:53,757
The boathouse is all bashed!
Holy crap!

38
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,966
Billy.

39
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:58,094
Sorry, Mom, but you just
gotta come! Come on!

40
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,554
Whoa!

41
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,056
Whoa.

42
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:03,058
- Whoa.
- Come on.

43
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:05,060
Having spoken,
the Doomsayer departs.

44
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:07,729
- BILLY: Come on!
- ( Stephanie chuckles )

45
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,814
How do you two always manage
to make me laugh?

46
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:13,526
- You have incredibly low standards.
- Mm-hmm.

47
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:16,613
Let's go, uh, see the damage.

48
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:17,697
No.

49
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,829
- Norton's tree.
- ( sighs ) Yeah.

50
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,249
You mean the dead one
I've been asking him

51
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,460
to take down for three years
before it finally blew over?

52
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,544
That tree?

53
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:35,799
- Really got smooshed.
- You ain't kiddin'.

54
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,843
Look at that.

55
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,305
What is it, Daddy?

56
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,307
Mist.

57
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,728
- On the lake?
- We've had mist on the lake before.

58
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:50,730
Coming off the mountain like that?

59
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:53,274
Two fronts meeting,

60
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,610
left over from the storm,
something like that.

61
00:03:55,694 --> 00:03:57,153
You sure?

62
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,655
Honey, I'm not the weatherman.

63
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,907
Why don't you take Billy,
get him dressed.

64
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,283
I'll take him to town with me.

65
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:03,743
Okay. Where you going?

66
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:06,913
I'm gonna go have a little chat
with our neighbor about his tree.

67
00:04:06,996 --> 00:04:08,081
Hon.

68
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:10,166
Don't worry, I'm not gonna
punch him in the nose.

69
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,543
You know what he's gonna say.

70
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:14,671
He's gonna say, "Sue me,"
which, I don't know, maybe we should.

71
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:19,217
Honey, one property dispute
with this guy is enough to last me a lifetime.

72
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:22,178
I'm gonna ask
for his insurance information.

73
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,055
- Okay.
- That's all.

74
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:25,432
Yeah.

75
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:28,059
( Norton grunting,
pulling chainsaw chain )

76
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:30,478
NORTON: Ohh!
Mother fucker!

77
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,066
Aw, shit!

78
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,652
Ohh, you mother fucker!

79
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:39,988
Cock sucker!

80
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,158
"Turn on.

81
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:45,410
"Full choke.

82
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:47,662
Pull five... choke."

83
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,585
I guess you've seen the--

84
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,171
Boathouse.

85
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,547
Yeah, and--?

86
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,257
Nothin'.

87
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,635
Just think we should trade
insurance info, you know?

88
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,762
That's all.

89
00:05:04,763 --> 00:05:06,347
( Scoffs )

90
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,975
Oh, my insurance guy's
gonna love me.

91
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:13,146
Oh.

92
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:15,190
Shit. The 1980.

93
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:17,108
NORTON: I was gonna bring
the station wagon, but...

94
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:22,739
I don't know, the weather was so beautiful
coming out of New York, I just-- you know, top down.

95
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:24,574
I'm sorry, man. I mean it.

96
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:26,117
Sincerely.

97
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:30,455
- That's nice of you to say.
- No, that car was cherry.

98
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:32,207
I hate to see it like that.

99
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,628
Okay, I'll tell you what,

100
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:39,506
I'll find my insurance guy's number,
I'll bring it by later.

101
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:41,132
- That okay?
- No problem.

102
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,473
So, uh, David--

103
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:53,645
You're not heading into town today
by any chance, are you?

104
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,079
DAVID:
Well, CMP's out in force.

105
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,747
Maybe we'll get our power back.

106
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:14,833
NORTON:
I know. Some storm, huh?

107
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,251
One for the books, yeah.

108
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:17,961
For a moment there last night,

109
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:20,463
I thought we were gonna take off
and head for Oz.

110
00:06:20,547 --> 00:06:22,590
WZON is off the air,

111
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:24,843
but Portland's still broadcasting.

112
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:27,804
- Daddy, look.
- Ah.

113
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,556
Guys from the base.

114
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,683
- From up the mountain?
- Uh-huh.

115
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:33,226
The Arrowhead Project?

116
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:37,772
Well, you're a local.
Any idea what they do up there?

117
00:06:37,856 --> 00:06:39,357
Missile defense research...

118
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,234
You know, I'm sure
you've heard the stories.

119
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:42,360
Oh, sure.

120
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,779
The woman at the Laundromat
says that, uh,

121
00:06:44,863 --> 00:06:47,991
they have a crashed flying saucer
up there with frozen alien bodies.

122
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,784
Right. Miss Edna. Yeah.

123
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:52,453
Miss Tabloid.
( chuckles )

124
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:55,206
"I Had Bigfoot's Baby."

125
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:59,043
"Satan's Face Appears
in Oil Well Fire."

126
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,461
You know, real reliable stuff.

127
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:06,676
DAVID:Well, they're in a hurry.

128
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,428
Maybe their power's out too.

129
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,646
Huh. Still no signal.

130
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:21,941
Why don't you go ahead?
I'm gonna try Steph on a pay phone.

131
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:23,693
Can I go with Mr. Norton, Daddy?

132
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:26,487
Sure, if you promise
to hold his hand, I guess.

133
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,614
- BILLY: Yeah.
- Yeah.

134
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,282
Here's a list.

135
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:30,700
- Sure.
- Okay?

136
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:32,035
Meet you guys in there.

137
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,288
Hold hands.

138
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:41,169
MAN: I'm sorry.
I didn't know it was your sister.

139
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:43,546
( Pulsing tone )

140
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,590
( Clicks phone cradle;
pulsing tone continues )

141
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:47,675
BOY:Those look <i>so</i> freaky!

142
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:48,801
Hmm.

143
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:56,559
( Chatter )

144
00:07:56,643 --> 00:07:58,436
- Sally, hey.
- Hey, Mr. Drayton.

145
00:07:58,519 --> 00:07:59,854
You guys look jammed up.

146
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:03,024
Yeah, well, half the staff
didn't show, plus the power's out.

147
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:05,443
Oh, no. What, no backup generator?

148
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:07,028
Only to keep the food cold.

149
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:09,989
Everything else, welcome to the Dark Ages,
and bring your checkbook.

150
00:08:10,073 --> 00:08:12,784
Hey, Thursday night,
Steph and I want a date night.

151
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,994
- Baby-sit?
- Heck, yeah. I'm there.

152
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:17,538
Oh, my God.

153
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,165
OLLIE: ( humorless chuckle )
The storm.

154
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:22,251
Everybody's stockin' up.
Been like this since we opened.

155
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:23,586
Crappy day, huh?

156
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:26,047
Eh, everyone's a little
pissed off this morning.

157
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:27,966
'Morning, Mrs. Carmody.

158
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:31,719
With lines like these,
I don't know how good it is,

159
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:34,013
but I guess we'll have to make do.

160
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:37,517
- Keep your head down, pal.
- I know it.

161
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:42,355
Hey, champ.

162
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,774
Your wife should be a doctor.

163
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:47,193
She could make a fortune
in Manhattan with this handwriting.

164
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:49,904
Yeah, it takes some getting used to.

165
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:52,115
Why don't you get your stuff?
I'll meet you at the checkout.

166
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,241
Okay, done.

167
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:59,122
Hey, David,
thanks for helping me out today.

168
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:05,378
Are you and Mr. Norton
gonna be friends now, Daddy?

169
00:09:05,461 --> 00:09:09,799
Oh, I don't know.
"Friends" might be stretching it a little.

170
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,219
I guess you're not mad
at each other anymore.

171
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:14,470
I guess not.

172
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:17,807
Hey. And that's a start, huh?

173
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,935
BUD: I'm sorry, ma'am,
the registers are down.

174
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,854
The power outage got us too.

175
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,606
Hopefully we'll have
power up pretty soon.

176
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:29,277
( Indistinct conversation )

177
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,362
( Chuckles )

178
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:38,119
- The bus leaves in 30 minutes.
- We'll make it, okay?

179
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:40,496
You guys get the goodies.
I'll wait in line.

180
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,542
BUD: Yes, ma'am, those are $1.25.

181
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:47,670
I need some change on register five.

182
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:51,090
Good morning, Ms. Reppler.

183
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:52,633
BILLY: Hello, Ms. Reppler.

184
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:56,929
Well, hello to you, Billy Drayton.
How'd you hold up in the storm?

185
00:09:57,013 --> 00:10:01,017
We had a tree come through the picture window
last night, right in my studio.

186
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,896
And the boathouse got all smooshed.
<i>Mr.</i> Norton's tree fell on it.

187
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,355
- IRENE: Ouch.
- Yeah.

188
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:09,025
IRENE:Sorry to hear that.

189
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,903
DAVID: How'd you guys make out?

190
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:15,156
HATTIE: Oh, we're fine.
It's the listings I'm worried about.

191
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:18,034
At the very least, I'll bet every one
of our "For Sale" signs fell over.

192
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:20,787
IRENE: We had damage
at the school, wouldn't you know?

193
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,831
That's what we get for not fixing
that roof when we should've,

194
00:10:23,915 --> 00:10:27,335
but with funds being cut every year...

195
00:10:27,418 --> 00:10:31,506
You'd think educating children
would be more of a priority in this country,

196
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,424
but you'd be wrong.

197
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:36,677
Government's got better things
to spend our money on,

198
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:40,389
like corporate handouts
and building bombs.

199
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:43,434
( Passing sirens wail )

200
00:10:49,941 --> 00:10:52,652
( Fire truck horn blares )

201
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,738
Daddy, is there a fire?
Is Mommy all right?

202
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:58,366
I'm sure she's fine.
Don't worry, okay?

203
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:00,910
Mind what you're doing, Sally.

204
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,538
SOLDIER: Oh, come on,
we got 10 days' leave.

205
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,664
Check our papers.

206
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,666
Look, I told you,
all leaves are cancelled.

207
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:07,792
I don't know why.

208
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,794
I gotta go check the pharmacy out.

209
00:11:09,877 --> 00:11:12,296
Three men meet me
back at the Jeep in five minutes.

210
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,631
That's an order.

211
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:19,470
Shit, man! Another half an hour,
and we'd have been gone.

212
00:11:23,641 --> 00:11:26,102
( Klaxon blares )

213
00:11:37,822 --> 00:11:41,284
( Klaxon continues )

214
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,255
Oh, my God!

215
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:03,973
Something in the mist!

216
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:07,435
- ( Excited shouting )
- Something in the mist took John Lee!

217
00:12:07,518 --> 00:12:08,853
Dan, catch your breath.

218
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,813
Something in the mist took John Lee.

219
00:12:10,897 --> 00:12:12,648
I could hear him screaming.

220
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:15,651
Shut the doors! Shut the doors!
My God!

221
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:17,361
Daddy, I'm scared.
Can we go home?

222
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,447
( Klaxon blares )

223
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:22,867
DAN: Don't go out there.

224
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,161
There's something in the mist.
It took John Lee.

225
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:27,747
MAN: Screw that!
I'm gettin' in my car.

226
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,290
Mister, no!

227
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:31,375
( Police siren wails )

228
00:12:32,501 --> 00:12:34,170
( Police siren ceases )

229
00:12:41,344 --> 00:12:42,595
( Keys jangling )

230
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:52,146
( Man screaming )

231
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:53,481
Oh, shit.

232
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:03,074
Please hold me.

233
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:05,159
- ( Billy whimpers )
- It's okay, it's okay.

234
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:09,330
CORNELL: It's a pollution cloud.
The mills down in Rumford.

235
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:12,541
Some kind of chemical explosion.
Has to be.

236
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,419
MAN: ( whispering )
What is it?

237
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:18,130
What's going on?

238
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,510
It's death.

239
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:24,553
Aah!

240
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:26,514
( Crashing and rumbling )

241
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,599
( Screaming and shouting )

242
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:42,405
( Screaming )

243
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:52,290
( Building girders groaning )

244
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:59,672
- ( Screaming and shouting )
- MAN: Stay down!

245
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:02,049
BILLY: Daddy!

246
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:04,218
( Rumbling stops )

247
00:14:04,302 --> 00:14:06,053
( Woman coughing )

248
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:08,723
( Woman weeping )

249
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:11,017
MAN: ( faintly )
You all right? You okay?

250
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,481
( Coughing )

251
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,737
That was an earthquake.

252
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:26,032
I tell you, the goddamn mills blew up!

253
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:29,577
OLLIE: Is everyone okay?
Is anyone hurt?

254
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,955
Everybody just stay put, okay?
Just stay inside the store.

255
00:14:33,039 --> 00:14:35,875
I can't. I can't stay here.
I gotta get home to my kids.

256
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:39,045
MRS. CARMODY: No.
No, don't go out there.

257
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,922
It's death out there.
It's the end of days.

258
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:44,008
Stop it, okay? Stop it.

259
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,927
NORTON: Please, everybody,
everybody just relax, okay?

260
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:48,971
He's right. Let's just stay cool.

261
00:14:49,055 --> 00:14:50,431
Let's just try to figure out
what happened.

262
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:54,894
I'm sorry, I-- I can't just stay here.
I have to get home to my kids.

263
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,854
Ma'am, no, you can't go out there.

264
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:58,647
Could be a poisonous gas cloud.

265
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,191
Didn't you hear that man screaming?

266
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,943
I agree. Let's stay here
until we figure it out.

267
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,362
WOMAN: You're not listening!

268
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,655
I can't stay here.

269
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:11,619
Wanda's looking after little Victor.
She's only eight.

270
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:15,998
Sometimes she forgets
she's supposed to be watching him.

271
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:21,921
I told them I'd only be gone
a few minutes.

272
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,383
She's only eight.

273
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,303
For their sakes, don't.

274
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:37,019
Well, isn't anybody gonna help me?

275
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:41,482
DAVID: ( softly ) Shh. It's okay, pal.

276
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:45,194
Won't somebody here see a lady home?

277
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,367
You?

278
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:00,042
You?

279
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:11,762
- DAVID: ( softly ) It's okay, buddy.
- You?

280
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:15,141
Ma'am, please,
I got my own boy to worry about.

281
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:21,772
I hope you all rot in hell.

282
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:24,066
OLLIE: Ma'am, please, wait until--

283
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:56,807
( Soft weeping )

284
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:01,729
BUD: Okay,
let's start cleaning up, okay?

285
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:04,440
Get the spilled bottles,
broken glass, stuff like that.

286
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:07,193
Aisle three has medical supplies.

287
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:10,070
- ( Billy crying )
- It's okay. It's okay.

288
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:11,780
All right, easy, champ.
Come on.

289
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:12,907
Come on.

290
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:15,659
Come on.
All right, hey, hey, hey.

291
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,411
Can't keep crying like this, pal.

292
00:17:17,495 --> 00:17:18,787
Come on!

293
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,873
Come on, you're gonna hurt yourself.

294
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:23,250
- Come on, are you all right?
- I want Mommy!

295
00:17:23,334 --> 00:17:24,835
All right, I know you want Mommy.

296
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:27,379
( Very softly )
All right, just try to breathe.

297
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:28,756
Just try to breathe, okay?

298
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:30,216
( Billy crying )

299
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:32,092
Just try to breathe, pal.
That's okay.

300
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,844
- ( Billy crying )
- It's all right.

301
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:39,558
I haven't seen him suck his thumb
like this since he was two years old.

302
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:41,435
AMANDA: He's in shock.

303
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:43,229
I think we all are.

304
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:45,022
IRENE: You haven't met.

305
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:46,565
Amanda Dunfrey.

306
00:17:46,649 --> 00:17:48,817
She's new in town
as of this semester.

307
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:51,278
Teaches third grade

308
00:17:51,362 --> 00:17:54,657
and the special ed kids,
now that Mosher's retired.

309
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,659
She's wonderful.
The kids love her.

310
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:59,787
And David's an artist.

311
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:02,790
He does movie posters and such.

312
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:03,916
And me...

313
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:09,380
Lord, I'm babbling away
like some old biddy at a tea party!

314
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:10,965
My nerves are jangled, I guess.

315
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:12,258
Boy settle down?

316
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,801
How is he?

317
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:14,969
Still hot.

318
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:16,762
Why don't I get him some aspirin.

319
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:18,472
- Aisle three.
- Okay.

320
00:18:18,556 --> 00:18:20,057
Thanks.

321
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,642
DAVID: How's Dan?

322
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:23,519
His nose stopped bleedin'.

323
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:25,938
He's calmer now.
Somebody gave him a Valium.

324
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:31,277
Can't believe the way he ran in here.
Never seen him like that.

325
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:35,364
I need something to cover my boy up.
Got any blankets?

326
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:37,575
Furniture pads. Loadin' dock.

327
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:40,703
Gonna keep checkin' on people.
If you need anything, just holler.

328
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,871
You bet. Sally, you mind?

329
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:45,291
Oh, I'd love to. I really should
help him clean up.

330
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:47,751
- I'll take him.
- Okay.

331
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:48,877
Daddy, don't go.

332
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:52,047
No, I'll be gone two seconds, Big Bill.
Come on, I'm gonna get your blanket.

333
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:54,008
Mrs. Reppler's here,

334
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,093
and so is Mrs. Turman.

335
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,637
I'll be close by, okay?

336
00:18:58,721 --> 00:19:01,307
- Okay.
- Don't worry, I'm not far. Okay?

337
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,392
Let me look at you.

338
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,313
Hmm?

339
00:19:09,023 --> 00:19:10,065
HATTIE: Wanna lie down?

340
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:11,191
Yeah.

341
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,527
There you go.

342
00:19:13,611 --> 00:19:17,239
NORTON: Soon as it blows away,
we can walk out of here safe <i>and</i> free,

343
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:18,741
but we have to be smart about it.

344
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:21,493
First thing we need to do
is keep our wits about us

345
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,953
and find out what's happened.

346
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:24,705
MAN: Well, how we gonna
do that, my man?

347
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:27,374
We've got no phone signal,
got no radio.

348
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:30,002
NORTON:I'm sure they're working
on those problems as we speak.

349
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:32,254
It stands to reason
that restoring communications

350
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:33,380
would be their top priority.

351
00:19:33,464 --> 00:19:35,466
( Machinery hums )

352
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:44,642
( David coughs )

353
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,312
( Coughing )
Jeez!

354
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,871
( Coughs )

355
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:10,000
Oh, <i>shit.</i>

356
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:13,003
- ( Sharp crack )
- Ow!

357
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:16,006
Shit!

358
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:18,342
( Grunts )

359
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,470
God <i>damn</i> it!

360
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:23,555
Ow! Ow!

361
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,767
Bitch!

362
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:27,976
NORTON: It's obvious that we're--

363
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,062
We're in some kind
of natural disaster here.

364
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:32,773
MAN: Ain't nothin' obvious
about this sombitch from where I sit.

365
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:35,109
CORNELL: There ain't nothin'
<i>natural</i> about it either.

366
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:36,235
MAN: That's right.

367
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,946
MRS. CARMODY: It's Judgment Day,
and it's come round at last.

368
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:41,532
There is nothing more obvious
or natural than that.

369
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:43,117
MAN: Ohh, fuck, now.

370
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:46,829
MRS. CARMODY: You've done that to yourself
by a life of sin and dissolution.

371
00:20:58,549 --> 00:21:00,884
( Metal rumbling and creaking )

372
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:03,804
( Rumbling and creaking cease )

373
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:13,147
( Metal rumbling and creaking )

374
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:20,320
( Creaking loudly )

375
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:34,835
Hey, whoa! David!

376
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:37,254
DAVID: Hey, you guys hear that?

377
00:21:37,337 --> 00:21:39,214
The generator?
We're just gonna check it out.

378
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:41,175
No, no, I turned the generator off.

379
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:43,260
It-- it was backing up.

380
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:47,264
- N-nobody else heard that sound?
- What sound?

381
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:51,935
I don't know, like a... weird noise,

382
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:53,771
back there in the dark.

383
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,356
Like something was, like,
pressing against the door.

384
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:59,943
Did you hear it
before the lights went out, or after?

385
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,862
No, only after.

386
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:04,198
After, but, look, I heard it, okay?

387
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,366
- Nobody's calling you a liar.
- That's what it sounds like.

388
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:09,077
JIM: No, no, no, no.
Now, don't be thattaway, Mr. Drayton.

389
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:11,246
You had a scare, no doubt.

390
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:13,749
What say we all go check it out? Here.

391
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:22,341
JIM: Oooopf!
( chuckles )

392
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,467
Man.

393
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:25,636
It's pretty rank in here.

394
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:27,846
- Myron, go check it out.
- All right.

395
00:22:30,808 --> 00:22:32,100
Go on, fire it up.

396
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,937
( Generator whirrs to life )

397
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:43,111
JIM: ( laughing )
All right!

398
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,279
Shut it off!

399
00:22:45,322 --> 00:22:47,074
Holy crow, don't that stink!

400
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:51,119
MYRON: Something's got
the exhaust vent plugged up from the outside.

401
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:53,580
You get it running long enough
to raise that door a little,

402
00:22:53,664 --> 00:22:55,165
I'll go out and clear
whatever's blockin' it.

403
00:22:55,249 --> 00:22:56,416
No, no, you can't do that.

404
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,460
MYRON: Why not?
It's an electric door, right?

405
00:22:58,544 --> 00:23:01,547
Well, yeah, but it may not be wise
to send him out there.

406
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:02,923
MYRON: Okay, I'll do it.

407
00:23:03,006 --> 00:23:04,925
No, look, it's not about
who goes out there.

408
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,969
What, don't you think I can do it?

409
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,680
Hey! I want to go!
It was my idea.

410
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:11,265
Well, wait, just stop, okay?

411
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:12,933
- J - Jim, right?
- JIM: Mm-hmm.

412
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:15,477
Myron? You guys are--

413
00:23:15,561 --> 00:23:17,646
You, well, you don't seem
to understand,

414
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:19,356
or you're tr yin' real hard not to.

415
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:21,024
This is no ordinary mist, okay?

416
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:24,278
You open that door,
and something gets in here.

417
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:25,612
NORM: Like what?

418
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,699
Well, like whatever
made that noise I heard.

419
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:30,284
Are you guys being willfully dense?

420
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:32,661
Mr. Drayton, you'll pardon me,

421
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:36,415
but I'm not convinced
that you heard anything.

422
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:39,543
I mean, we're not hearing
anything now, right? Anybody?

423
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:43,005
See? ( chuckles )

424
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:46,091
Now, I know, I know--
you're a big shot artist

425
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:48,635
with connections in New York
and Hollywood and all like that,

426
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:51,013
but that don't make you better
than anybody else, not in my book.

427
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:52,472
Hey, I didn't say that.

428
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:54,850
Nor do I like being
talked down to or called stupid

429
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,895
by a guy who went to college,
just 'cause he's got the jitters.

430
00:23:57,978 --> 00:24:00,147
Fellas, it doesn't even matter
about the generator.

431
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,565
The food'll keep without it.

432
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:06,069
Kid, I'm gonna start the motor, you raise the door,
and you yell out when you got enough room.

433
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:07,696
Yeah. Okay, good.

434
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:09,531
DAVID: Wait.

435
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:12,618
This is-- you guys gonna let
this kid risk his life

436
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:14,369
over a generator
that doesn't even matter?

437
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:15,829
Would you just
shut the fuck up already?

438
00:24:15,913 --> 00:24:16,955
OLLIE: Norm!

439
00:24:17,039 --> 00:24:18,999
JIM:Listen, Mr. Drayton,
I tell you what.

440
00:24:19,082 --> 00:24:22,502
The next time you got somethin' to say,
you count your teeth,

441
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:25,881
because I'm sick to death
of your bullshit.

442
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:28,425
All right? Come on, Myron.

443
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:30,260
- DAVID: This is crazy!
- OLLIE: Leave 'em be.

444
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:32,304
What am I, impugning
their manhood or something?

445
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:34,848
Listen, they've lost
their sense of proportion.

446
00:24:34,932 --> 00:24:36,266
What's going on here?

447
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:38,185
Out there in the market,
they were scared and confused.

448
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:40,187
In here, there's a problem
they can solve,

449
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:42,272
so they're goddamn gonna solve it.

450
00:24:42,356 --> 00:24:43,857
- MYRON: Ready, kid?
- Let's rock.

451
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:45,275
Norm, come on.

452
00:24:45,359 --> 00:24:46,401
Don't, man.

453
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:49,655
( Generator whirrs to life )

454
00:24:50,739 --> 00:24:51,907
DAVID: It's a mistake.

455
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:57,663
Pussy.

456
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:03,293
Go up!

457
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:26,608
So...

458
00:25:26,692 --> 00:25:28,151
any boogeymen?

459
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:29,736
( Jim laughs )

460
00:25:31,071 --> 00:25:32,572
JIM:Pretty scary, ain't it, Norm?

461
00:25:32,656 --> 00:25:34,700
Yeah, right.

462
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:36,952
( laughter )

463
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:38,996
MYRON: Norm.

464
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:41,707
Norm!

465
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:43,083
What the fuck!

466
00:25:43,166 --> 00:25:44,710
Ahh! Get it off! Get it off!

467
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,670
Get this friggin' thing off me!

468
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:48,588
Get it off! Help me!

469
00:25:48,672 --> 00:25:50,340
Help me! Help me!

470
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:51,883
Aah! Aaahhh!

471
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:53,135
Jesus!

472
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:57,097
( Norm shouting )

473
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:06,606
There's more! There's more!

474
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:08,608
Somebody help me.

475
00:26:09,609 --> 00:26:12,112
Somebody help me.

476
00:26:12,195 --> 00:26:13,864
What the fuck are you waitin' for?

477
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:15,907
( Norm crying and shouting )

478
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:21,663
Aaahhhh!

479
00:26:26,293 --> 00:26:27,669
Hang on!

480
00:26:29,171 --> 00:26:31,381
Aaahhhh!

481
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:40,557
Hold him still!
Hold him still!

482
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:45,395
Aaahhhh!

483
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:50,567
Oh, Jesus!

484
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:55,155
( Norm grunting and straining )

485
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:08,752
( Monster sniffing )

486
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:16,343
MYRON: Aah!

487
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:18,804
Aah!

488
00:27:23,934 --> 00:27:25,602
JIM: Shit! Oh, shit!

489
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:27,771
Oh, shit!

490
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:31,733
OLLIE: David, it's no good!

491
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:32,859
Aah!

492
00:27:32,943 --> 00:27:34,361
DAVID:Start the generator.

493
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:37,030
Aah! Aaaggghhh!

494
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:49,793
Gaaahhhh!

495
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:57,551
( Norm screams )

496
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:19,114
( Monster shrieks )

497
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:44,890
Hey, I'm sorry.

498
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:51,188
I mean, how the-- how the hell
was I supposed to know what you meant?

499
00:28:52,647 --> 00:28:54,191
You said you <i>heard</i> something.

500
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:57,027
How was I supposed to know
what you meant?

501
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:58,320
You should've said
what you meant better.

502
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:01,448
I don't know, I thought maybe
it was a big bird or some--

503
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:04,326
You got that kid killed!

504
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:06,369
Did you get a good look at it? Huh?

505
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:09,581
Did you get a good look
at what you did?

506
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:10,874
- Huh?
- David!

507
00:29:10,957 --> 00:29:12,292
Don't hit him anymore!
Doesn't solve anything!

508
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:15,128
You two assholes,
you got that kid killed!

509
00:29:15,212 --> 00:29:17,214
And I got his fuckin' blood on me!

510
00:29:20,217 --> 00:29:22,761
( Groaning )

511
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:31,061
( David panting )

512
00:29:37,067 --> 00:29:39,110
Okay, I'm done.

513
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:42,239
Okay.

514
00:29:45,825 --> 00:29:48,870
- What's next?
- Kill the generator.

515
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,122
That's the first thing.

516
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:56,294
JIM: I'm sorry.

517
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:03,051
DAVID: Jesus Christ! Oh, God!

518
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:05,720
JIM: I'm-- I'm sorry about the kid.

519
00:30:07,764 --> 00:30:09,933
Oh, God. Oh, God. Oh, God.

520
00:30:11,309 --> 00:30:12,686
We oughta get out of here.

521
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:15,105
( Coughing and retching )

522
00:30:17,107 --> 00:30:18,400
Hey, we didn't twist his arm.

523
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:21,778
Yeah, he's a fuckin' kid.
He's supposed to be stupid.

524
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:24,656
What's your excuse, huh?

525
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:29,202
Get outta here.

526
00:30:30,287 --> 00:30:32,205
Go back in the market.
Stay by the door.

527
00:30:34,457 --> 00:30:36,418
Don't say anything, to anybody.

528
00:30:37,961 --> 00:30:39,004
Not yet.

529
00:30:40,547 --> 00:30:41,589
Not yet.

530
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:49,514
( Generator whirrs )

531
00:30:52,142 --> 00:30:53,601
( Generator stops )

532
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:58,023
OLLIE: ( softly ) Shit.

533
00:30:58,106 --> 00:31:00,942
David? Need a little light here.

534
00:31:11,745 --> 00:31:13,538
We have to tell 'em.

535
00:31:13,621 --> 00:31:16,499
The people in the market,
we have to stop 'em going outside.

536
00:31:17,751 --> 00:31:19,085
They won't believe us.

537
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:21,421
They have to.

538
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,715
I'm not sure I believe it.
I was <i>here.</i>

539
00:31:24,758 --> 00:31:26,843
W-What we saw was impossible.

540
00:31:26,926 --> 00:31:28,803
You know that, don't you?

541
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:29,929
I mean, what--

542
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:32,932
What do we say?

543
00:31:33,933 --> 00:31:36,603
How do we convince them?

544
00:31:39,606 --> 00:31:43,610
Ollie, what the hell were
those tentacles even attached to?

545
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:51,576
Oh, my God!
Are-- are you all right?

546
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:54,287
DAVID: Shh! Yeah, yeah, yeah,
it's not my blood. I'm fine.

547
00:31:54,371 --> 00:31:55,747
W-What the hell happened?

548
00:31:55,830 --> 00:31:59,709
I'll explain. Give me a minute, okay?
I need to deal with something first.

549
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:03,213
Please, I've got to--

550
00:32:03,296 --> 00:32:05,965
I can't let Billy see me like this.
He's scared enough.

551
00:32:06,049 --> 00:32:08,968
Just give me a minute.
Keep him distracted. Okay?

552
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,095
Okay.

553
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:18,645
JIM: Hey, look,
I'm sorry about Norm.

554
00:32:18,728 --> 00:32:20,146
Me too.

555
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:22,565
I mean, I ain't makin' excuses,
I'm just ea yin'.

556
00:32:22,649 --> 00:32:23,942
Look, we need to tell people.

557
00:32:24,025 --> 00:32:26,486
No need to say how it went down
or anything like that,

558
00:32:26,569 --> 00:32:29,322
but, uh, we're in the deep shit here.

559
00:32:29,406 --> 00:32:30,907
People need to know.

560
00:32:30,990 --> 00:32:32,492
MYRON:
What about the out-of-towners?

561
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:35,328
We got plenty of them in the store.
Where do we even start?

562
00:32:35,412 --> 00:32:37,664
- OLLIE: Brent Norton?
- JIM: That windbag?

563
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,458
He's an important attorney in New York.

564
00:32:40,542 --> 00:32:42,669
That fellow could be
on the bench one day.

565
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:45,255
Counts a lot with people of this town,
or-- or anywhere.

566
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:46,881
- MYRON: Yeah, that's right.
- Do it quick, David.

567
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:49,843
We've got to discuss how we're gonna
stop that thing getting in here.

568
00:32:49,926 --> 00:32:51,719
W-wait. What do you mean getting in?

569
00:32:52,429 --> 00:32:53,930
You shut the loading door.

570
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:57,434
Yeah, but the entire front of the store
is plate glass.

571
00:33:01,312 --> 00:33:03,273
Jesus Christ.

572
00:33:13,867 --> 00:33:15,660
NORTON: I was wondering
where you'd gotten to.

573
00:33:15,743 --> 00:33:17,203
DAVID: Um, listen...

574
00:33:17,287 --> 00:33:20,081
that guy that came in here,
the one with the bloody nose...

575
00:33:20,165 --> 00:33:22,834
( conversation continues indistinctly )

576
00:33:25,587 --> 00:33:29,090
...they're-- they're--
We saw <i>tentacles.</i>

577
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:32,469
- Ain't goin' very well, is it?
- Unh-unh.

578
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:35,722
- You... what?
- Come here, you've got--

579
00:33:36,931 --> 00:33:38,141
Come here.

580
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:41,186
Tell him.

581
00:33:43,313 --> 00:33:44,355
It's true.

582
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,490
Tentacles. Yeah.

583
00:34:02,665 --> 00:34:04,167
Um, gentlemen, um...

584
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:07,962
I'm sorry, I--
I'm just not that stupid.

585
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:11,257
I mean, what do you take me for?
I'm shocked.

586
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:13,301
I'm shocked.

587
00:34:13,384 --> 00:34:17,555
I'm shocked. It's pretty tasteless using what's
happening here to try to make me look like an idiot.

588
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:19,265
No, no, that's not
what's going on here.

589
00:34:19,349 --> 00:34:21,309
Look, come back
to the loading dock, okay?

590
00:34:21,392 --> 00:34:22,435
I'll show you.

591
00:34:22,519 --> 00:34:26,022
Blood. A chunk of tentacle
on-- on the floor.

592
00:34:26,105 --> 00:34:27,148
No.

593
00:34:27,232 --> 00:34:28,942
No? What do you mean no?

594
00:34:29,025 --> 00:34:31,277
No. We've got real problems
to deal with here,

595
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:36,407
and this pathetic attempt at a joke
has gone far enough.

596
00:34:36,491 --> 00:34:39,452
<i>Mr.</i> Norton, what reason
could we possibly have--?

597
00:34:39,536 --> 00:34:41,162
Oh, please! Please!

598
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:43,706
This is payback for the lawsuit
that I filed against him last year,

599
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:45,625
and you guys are backing him up.

600
00:34:45,708 --> 00:34:47,335
So winning wasn't enough, huh?

601
00:34:47,418 --> 00:34:49,629
You wanted to humiliate me some more,

602
00:34:49,712 --> 00:34:52,048
show me a rubber snake
while these-- these hicks

603
00:34:52,131 --> 00:34:53,424
stand around laughing their asses off.

604
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:55,426
- Watch who you callin' a hick!
- Myron! Myron!

605
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,220
- Hey, hey, fuck--!
- JIM:Mr. Norton, I swear,

606
00:34:57,303 --> 00:34:59,389
you have got us all wrong.

607
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:03,977
You're not too crazy about,
um, out-of-towners, are you?

608
00:35:04,978 --> 00:35:07,021
I only spend my money,
and I pay my taxes here,

609
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:10,984
and I have seen <i>you</i>
talking behind my back.

610
00:35:12,527 --> 00:35:14,028
Y'all stick together.

611
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:18,825
Well, don't I feel foolish?

612
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:21,369
I actually thought you were
being kind to me today,

613
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:22,954
and, well, thanks
for setting me straight.

614
00:35:23,037 --> 00:35:25,164
And I'm glad that tree fell
on your boathouse, you know that?

615
00:35:25,248 --> 00:35:27,667
Glad. Smashed it in
pretty good, didn't it? Fantastic.

616
00:35:27,750 --> 00:35:29,335
Now, all of y'all,
just stay out of my way.

617
00:35:29,419 --> 00:35:31,963
I know you're scared, man.
I'm scared too.

618
00:35:32,046 --> 00:35:34,090
- Lives are at stake around here.
- David--

619
00:35:34,173 --> 00:35:36,509
Okay, my <i>son's</i> life.
Now, I need <i>you.</i>

620
00:35:36,593 --> 00:35:40,138
Brent, please, get your head out of your ass.

621
00:35:40,221 --> 00:35:43,391
All right, I'll drag you back there
if I have to. Come here.

622
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:46,394
David, get-- get your goddamn hands off of me!

623
00:35:46,477 --> 00:35:48,438
I'll sue your ass again!

624
00:35:48,521 --> 00:35:50,773
Sue your ass, and this time
you'll go to jail!

625
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:52,358
This man assaulted me.

626
00:35:52,442 --> 00:35:54,986
He assaulted me.
You were witness to it.

627
00:35:55,069 --> 00:35:56,112
This man's crazy.
He's crazy.

628
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:57,780
No.

629
00:35:57,864 --> 00:36:00,283
He isn't. I wish he was, but he isn't.

630
00:36:00,366 --> 00:36:02,410
( Scoffs )

631
00:36:02,493 --> 00:36:06,623
E-everyone in the store,
you want to come back here?

632
00:36:07,665 --> 00:36:10,335
There's something you need to hear.
It concerns you all.

633
00:36:10,418 --> 00:36:11,669
Okay.

634
00:36:11,753 --> 00:36:14,714
BUD: W-w-wait. I don't know
what you people think you're doing.

635
00:36:14,797 --> 00:36:16,341
You're drinking?

636
00:36:16,424 --> 00:36:17,884
For Christ's sake, Ollie.

637
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:21,971
Do you want me to report you?
You want to lose your job?

638
00:36:22,055 --> 00:36:23,973
Look, I'm gonna be taking down names,
starting with you.

639
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:26,017
And I am prepared to file
a police report.

640
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:28,061
- Fine, Bud, write down your names.
- I will.

641
00:36:28,144 --> 00:36:30,980
But in the meantime,
shut the fuck up and listen.

642
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:33,983
This is Mr. David Drayton.

643
00:36:34,067 --> 00:36:37,403
You need to hear what he's got to say
if you're thinking about leaving.

644
00:36:37,487 --> 00:36:39,113
DAVID: ...go hang out
with the ladies, all right?

645
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,531
Listen, don't be scared.

646
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:43,743
It's okay.

647
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:46,954
Okay.

648
00:36:48,081 --> 00:36:49,415
This is how it is.

649
00:36:49,499 --> 00:36:51,918
Now, I don't know
what this mist is...

650
00:36:52,919 --> 00:36:55,129
but there are things in it,
and they're dangerous, like Dan said.

651
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,255
That's right.

652
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:58,633
That's exactly right.

653
00:36:58,716 --> 00:37:00,593
MAN: What kind of things?

654
00:37:00,677 --> 00:37:02,595
I never saw it.
It happened too fast.

655
00:37:02,679 --> 00:37:04,514
I got knocked down.

656
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,766
Five of us went back
in the loading dock.

657
00:37:06,849 --> 00:37:10,436
It was Jim, Myron, Ollie...

658
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,105
me...

659
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,731
Norm, the bag boy.

660
00:37:13,815 --> 00:37:15,274
- We opened the door...
- Where's Norm?

661
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:19,070
...so Norm could go out
and clear the vent for the generator.

662
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:22,407
Something come out of the mist
and took him.

663
00:37:22,490 --> 00:37:24,784
- Took him?
- What do you mean?

664
00:37:26,327 --> 00:37:27,495
Just... killed him.

665
00:37:27,578 --> 00:37:29,455
I mean dragged him off.

666
00:37:29,539 --> 00:37:34,085
Now, guys, I don't know
what these things are.

667
00:37:35,128 --> 00:37:36,629
All we saw were tentacles.

668
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:39,507
( Onlookers muttering )

669
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:41,551
WOMAN: <i>Tentacles?</i>

670
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:46,347
NORTON: Tentacles, he says.

671
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:48,975
Tentacles from Planet X.

672
00:37:49,058 --> 00:37:50,393
It's a lie, you know.

673
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:53,646
I mean, all these people do
is just lie each other up.

674
00:37:53,730 --> 00:37:54,897
It's a pile of shit.

675
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:58,234
Of course it's a lie.
Of course it's a lie. It's lunacy.

676
00:37:58,317 --> 00:38:01,154
From the look of it, the tentacles
are coming out of the beer cans.

677
00:38:01,237 --> 00:38:04,031
All right, uh, Bud,
don't take our word for it. Go look.

678
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:11,706
DAVID: ( softly )
Over there.

679
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:18,880
What the hell is that?

680
00:38:30,892 --> 00:38:32,393
( Sizzling sound )

681
00:38:51,329 --> 00:38:54,665
It appears we may have a problem
of some magnitude here.

682
00:39:10,765 --> 00:39:12,475
Yeah, just keep 'em in line. Thanks.

683
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:25,029
Let me...

684
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:30,576
help these people.

685
00:39:30,660 --> 00:39:32,453
Let me--

686
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:34,539
let me preach Your word.

687
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:38,960
Let me shine Your light,

688
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:41,546
'cause they're not <i>all</i> bad.

689
00:39:42,547 --> 00:39:44,882
They can't <i>all</i> be bad.

690
00:39:47,885 --> 00:39:51,806
Some can be saved, can't they?

691
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:53,641
Yes.

692
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,351
Some <i>can</i> be brought...

693
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:59,480
to heaven's holy gates
through Your grace.

694
00:39:59,564 --> 00:40:00,773
I have to believe that,

695
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:05,278
though I know most will swim
in the lake of fire forever.

696
00:40:08,906 --> 00:40:10,575
If I can save a few...

697
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:13,911
even one...

698
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:17,415
then my life will have counted
for something.

699
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:21,252
I will have pulled my weight.

700
00:40:21,335 --> 00:40:24,714
I will have earned my place at Your side.

701
00:40:24,797 --> 00:40:29,051
I will have served a purpose
here on this earth.

702
00:40:29,135 --> 00:40:30,136
Hello?

703
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:43,774
( Mrs. Carmody sniffles softly )

704
00:40:46,777 --> 00:40:48,070
What?

705
00:40:48,154 --> 00:40:50,364
I just need to use the bathroom.

706
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:51,490
Oh.

707
00:40:52,617 --> 00:40:55,036
Okay. Well, then, have at it.

708
00:40:59,332 --> 00:41:00,583
Ma'am...

709
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:05,504
I-- I just want you to know
that it's okay--

710
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:07,214
Being scared, I mean--

711
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:09,842
And, well, if you need a friend--

712
00:41:09,926 --> 00:41:12,345
You know, someone to talk to.

713
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:14,430
I have a friend--

714
00:41:14,513 --> 00:41:18,392
God up above.
I talk to Him every day.

715
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:20,478
Don't you condescend to me.

716
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:21,687
I'm sorry?

717
00:41:21,771 --> 00:41:25,316
Not ever.
You don't mock me.

718
00:41:25,399 --> 00:41:26,984
That's not what I was doing.

719
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:29,987
Well, I'll tell you what--

720
00:41:30,071 --> 00:41:32,073
The day I need a friend like you,

721
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:36,077
I'll just have myself a little squat
and shit one out.

722
00:41:40,915 --> 00:41:42,541
Maybe you <i>do</i> believe this.

723
00:41:42,625 --> 00:41:45,711
Maybe they're not lies,
they're delusions. Whatever.

724
00:41:45,795 --> 00:41:49,006
Uh, the fact remains,
the evidence here is flimsy.

725
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:51,842
- It's bordering on ludicrous.
- Hey, this isn't a courtroom.

726
00:41:51,926 --> 00:41:54,762
You're not arguing a case, and you're doing
nothing but damage, talking the way you are.

727
00:41:54,845 --> 00:41:57,890
And you can throw as much cow's blood
around the loading dock as you want to.

728
00:41:57,974 --> 00:42:00,351
- You still haven't fooled anyone.
- OLLIE: Leave it alone, David.

729
00:42:00,434 --> 00:42:02,228
You can't convince
some people there's a fire

730
00:42:02,311 --> 00:42:04,271
even when their hair is burning.

731
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:05,856
Denial is a powerful thing.

732
00:42:05,940 --> 00:42:06,983
Well, keep talking.

733
00:42:07,066 --> 00:42:10,319
I'll have no part of it,
nor would any thinking person.

734
00:42:10,403 --> 00:42:13,072
Keep thinking, Mr. Lawyer.

735
00:42:13,155 --> 00:42:16,117
There's no defense
against the will of God.

736
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:18,411
There's no court of appeals in hell.

737
00:42:18,494 --> 00:42:20,830
There's no defense here, either.

738
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:25,710
Not even with all the fertilizer in the world,
not even if you stack it as high as you can.

739
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:28,129
It's still just bags of shit, isn't it?

740
00:42:28,212 --> 00:42:30,506
Those of you who want to discuss
this thing rationally

741
00:42:30,589 --> 00:42:34,468
to find a means of rescue
are welcome to join me.

742
00:42:34,552 --> 00:42:37,263
Those who want to stack dog food...

743
00:42:37,346 --> 00:42:38,973
knock yourselves out.

744
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:44,937
We got those windows taped up
as best we could.

745
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:46,147
It should help.

746
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:47,565
Yeah, think so?

747
00:42:49,608 --> 00:42:51,444
Duct tape and dog food bags.

748
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:54,989
That bad?

749
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:56,115
It's not good.

750
00:42:56,198 --> 00:42:59,285
There's none so blind
as those who will not see.

751
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:02,121
Open your eyes.

752
00:43:02,204 --> 00:43:04,457
Let the scales fall away.

753
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:06,542
This has all been written.

754
00:43:08,044 --> 00:43:11,422
Revelations, chapter 15:

755
00:43:11,505 --> 00:43:13,799
"And the temple was filled with smoke

756
00:43:13,883 --> 00:43:16,052
"from the glory of God

757
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:17,470
"and from His power,

758
00:43:17,553 --> 00:43:19,513
"and no one could enter the temple

759
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:23,142
until the seven plagues
of the seven angels were completed."

760
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:25,519
Well, what are you saying?

761
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:26,937
What are you proposing?

762
00:43:27,021 --> 00:43:28,564
That we all prepare...

763
00:43:30,066 --> 00:43:31,484
to meet our Maker.

764
00:43:31,567 --> 00:43:33,736
JIM:Oh, prepare to meet shit!

765
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:37,281
Lady, your tongue
must be hung in the middle

766
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:39,241
so that it can waggle at both ends.

767
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:41,077
MRS. CARMODY:
The end time has come,

768
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,870
not in flames, but in mist.

769
00:43:42,953 --> 00:43:43,996
JIM: Come here!

770
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:45,206
MYRON: Easy! Back off!

771
00:43:45,289 --> 00:43:48,667
How about if your ass prepares
to meet my size-10 work boot.

772
00:43:48,751 --> 00:43:51,212
- How about that?
- Hey, there's no call for that.

773
00:43:51,295 --> 00:43:53,547
Myron, please,
calm your friend down.

774
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:56,425
MRS. CARMODY: I'm trying
to save your soul, you stupid man.

775
00:43:56,509 --> 00:43:58,719
- Doubters will doubt till the end.
- It's okay.

776
00:43:58,803 --> 00:43:59,845
No, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

777
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:02,515
A monstrosity <i>did</i> pull
that poor boy away.

778
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:06,435
Things in the mist--
do you doubt?

779
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:07,561
Do you?

780
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:10,981
Then go out.

781
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:13,442
Go out and say,
"How do you do."

782
00:44:13,526 --> 00:44:14,568
Shut up, lady.

783
00:44:16,237 --> 00:44:17,404
For God's sakes.

784
00:44:17,488 --> 00:44:19,657
Look, you'll have to stop now.
You're scaring the children.

785
00:44:19,740 --> 00:44:21,158
They should be scared.

786
00:44:21,242 --> 00:44:23,911
Oh, yes, they should.

787
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:27,414
Their beautiful, pure little minds

788
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:29,917
have been corrupted with lies.

789
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,043
Lies.

790
00:44:31,127 --> 00:44:33,212
All this talk of a modern God,

791
00:44:33,295 --> 00:44:36,006
or no God.

792
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:37,758
There is one God.

793
00:44:37,842 --> 00:44:39,468
The God of the Israelites.

794
00:44:39,552 --> 00:44:42,388
And He is a stern and vengeful God,

795
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:45,015
and we have been mocking Him
far too long,

796
00:44:45,099 --> 00:44:48,727
and now He demands
retribution in blood.

797
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:51,480
It is time to declare yourselves.

798
00:44:51,564 --> 00:44:53,232
Take sides--

799
00:44:53,315 --> 00:44:55,109
The saved and the damned.

800
00:44:55,192 --> 00:44:58,696
Read the Good Book.
It calls for expiation.

801
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:00,656
- Blood!
- What?

802
00:45:00,739 --> 00:45:01,782
Blood.

803
00:45:02,867 --> 00:45:04,535
Little Normie was first,

804
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:07,663
and now God calls the rest of us.

805
00:45:07,746 --> 00:45:09,248
The bill is due.

806
00:45:09,331 --> 00:45:10,791
It must be paid.

807
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:13,878
As Abraham prepared
to sacrifice his only son

808
00:45:13,961 --> 00:45:15,838
to prove his love for God, so--

809
00:45:15,921 --> 00:45:17,339
- Enough.
- ( onlookers gasp )

810
00:45:22,887 --> 00:45:25,389
- Ohh.
- Another down payment.

811
00:45:25,472 --> 00:45:27,391
A few more pennies in the jar.

812
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,977
Now, that's nice, see.
I can't smack her, but it's okay for you.

813
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:31,353
I-I'm sorry everybody,

814
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:34,440
but this lady's perspective is
a little too Old Testament for my taste.

815
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:36,025
MRS. CARMODY:
They'll come for you.

816
00:45:37,026 --> 00:45:39,528
Maybe tonight,
when darkness comes.

817
00:45:41,071 --> 00:45:43,949
They'll come tonight,
and they'll take someone else.

818
00:45:44,033 --> 00:45:46,035
See if they don't.

819
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:47,870
And when they do,

820
00:45:47,953 --> 00:45:50,539
you will cry to God,

821
00:45:50,623 --> 00:45:54,293
and you will beg Mother Carmody
to show you the way.

822
00:45:54,376 --> 00:45:55,711
OLLIE: That's fine.

823
00:45:56,754 --> 00:45:59,006
But until then,
if you don't shut up,

824
00:45:59,089 --> 00:46:01,091
I'll wrap this tape around your mouth.

825
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:03,469
You just try it, Ollie Weeks.

826
00:46:03,552 --> 00:46:05,054
And you, bitch...

827
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:08,057
you hit me again...

828
00:46:09,099 --> 00:46:11,143
if you dare.

829
00:46:11,227 --> 00:46:13,896
You'll be on your knees to me
before this is through.

830
00:46:20,611 --> 00:46:25,324
Those of you who aren't local should know
that Mrs. Carmody is known in town for being...

831
00:46:26,408 --> 00:46:27,618
unstable.

832
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:30,871
No shit.
What was your first clue?

833
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,417
SOLDIER: Shh.

834
00:46:36,502 --> 00:46:39,421
- Hi.
- What's up, little dude?

835
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:41,340
How come your friends
don't come get us?

836
00:46:41,423 --> 00:46:42,967
They got tanks and stuff, right?

837
00:46:44,426 --> 00:46:45,844
Why can't you just call 'em?

838
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:47,012
Phones don't work.

839
00:46:47,096 --> 00:46:48,889
But don't you got, like, a radio?

840
00:46:48,973 --> 00:46:50,432
Hey, champ, what's going on?

841
00:46:50,516 --> 00:46:52,685
I want their friends
to come rescue us.

842
00:46:52,768 --> 00:46:54,895
They would if they could, pal.
They're stuck here just like us.

843
00:46:54,979 --> 00:46:55,813
- But--
- Shh.

844
00:46:55,896 --> 00:46:57,648
Now, guys, we could use
a hand over there.

845
00:46:57,731 --> 00:46:58,774
SOLDIER: Yeah, sure thing.

846
00:46:58,857 --> 00:47:00,567
SOLDIER #2:
Troop, off your asses.

847
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:03,404
- DAVID: You all right?
- I don't like that scary lady.

848
00:47:03,487 --> 00:47:05,823
Oh, man, I don't either.

849
00:47:05,906 --> 00:47:07,366
But you know what?

850
00:47:08,367 --> 00:47:10,160
Maybe she's scared too.

851
00:47:11,203 --> 00:47:12,246
You think?

852
00:47:13,247 --> 00:47:14,707
You think Mommy's okay?

853
00:47:15,708 --> 00:47:18,043
( Sighs ) Billy...

854
00:47:20,963 --> 00:47:23,048
I'm sorry about the times
I was bad to her.

855
00:47:23,132 --> 00:47:24,174
Aw, hey.

856
00:47:25,217 --> 00:47:28,304
Mommy loves you very much.

857
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:29,888
And I'll bet she's fine.

858
00:47:31,724 --> 00:47:33,726
And I promise you,

859
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:36,979
I'm gonna do everything I can
to get us back to her.

860
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:39,982
- Okay?
- 'Kay.

861
00:47:40,983 --> 00:47:42,443
- Yeah?
- 'Kay.

862
00:47:43,485 --> 00:47:47,531
So, we can use the charcoal fluid
and the mops to make torches.

863
00:47:47,614 --> 00:47:49,616
And we've got knives and stuff, God knows.

864
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:54,913
This may be a silly question, Bud,
but... do you happen to have a <i>gun</i> in the store?

865
00:47:55,914 --> 00:47:57,750
Here? No. Please.

866
00:47:57,833 --> 00:47:59,585
This-- this isn't Los Angeles.

867
00:47:59,668 --> 00:48:01,295
I've got a shotgun in my truck.

868
00:48:02,671 --> 00:48:04,089
I could try for it if you want.

869
00:48:04,173 --> 00:48:06,467
Oh, God, I don't think that'd be
a good idea, <i>Mr.</i> Cornell.

870
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:07,593
Hold on.

871
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:11,513
This gun, um...

872
00:48:11,597 --> 00:48:13,432
my husband's idea.

873
00:48:13,515 --> 00:48:15,517
He's away on business a lot.

874
00:48:15,601 --> 00:48:16,769
It's not even loaded.

875
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:18,479
Ain't much use unloaded, ma'am.

876
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:19,605
AMANDA: Um...

877
00:48:23,192 --> 00:48:24,735
DAVID:
You know how to use that?

878
00:48:24,818 --> 00:48:28,572
Well, I shot it once on a pistol range.
Hit the target a few times.

879
00:48:28,655 --> 00:48:31,450
So, we got a gun.

880
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:33,452
Anybody know how to shoot it?

881
00:48:33,535 --> 00:48:34,912
<i>Well,</i> I mean?

882
00:48:34,995 --> 00:48:36,038
I do.

883
00:48:38,791 --> 00:48:39,833
You?

884
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:42,669
( Scoffs )
Ollie. Please.

885
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:49,927
Some target shooting.

886
00:48:50,010 --> 00:48:52,179
State champion in '94.

887
00:48:52,262 --> 00:48:55,891
- MAN:You're crazy if you go out there!
- NORTON: Let us pass! Let us pass, please!

888
00:48:55,974 --> 00:48:57,184
Let's just talk this thing through.

889
00:48:57,267 --> 00:48:59,520
NORTON: We have, and we've
made our decision. We're leaving.

890
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:02,523
Hey, Mr. Mackey's gonna barbecue
some chicken on the gas grill.

891
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:04,900
- Why don't we just sit down and just--
- What, and let you keep on talking?

892
00:49:04,983 --> 00:49:07,111
No, I've been in far too many
courtrooms to fall for that.

893
00:49:07,194 --> 00:49:09,238
You've already psyched out
half a dozen of my people already.

894
00:49:09,321 --> 00:49:10,364
AMANDA: <i>Your</i> people?

895
00:49:10,447 --> 00:49:12,241
What kind of talk is that?
They're people, that's all.

896
00:49:12,324 --> 00:49:13,784
Now-- now listen, everyone.

897
00:49:13,867 --> 00:49:16,829
We are experiencing
some kind of disaster.

898
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:18,872
I don't know whether
it's manmade or natural,

899
00:49:18,956 --> 00:49:22,835
but I do know that
it's definitely not supernatural

900
00:49:22,918 --> 00:49:25,254
or biblical,
and, no offense, Mrs. Carmody,

901
00:49:25,337 --> 00:49:26,964
but the only way
we're gonna help ourselves

902
00:49:27,047 --> 00:49:28,674
is to seek rescue.

903
00:49:30,509 --> 00:49:31,552
We're going out.

904
00:49:34,221 --> 00:49:36,265
- Brent, look.
- I'm not discussing this any further.

905
00:49:36,348 --> 00:49:38,517
I know. I just want to ask a favor.

906
00:49:40,227 --> 00:49:41,770
Tie this around your waist.

907
00:49:41,854 --> 00:49:42,938
What for?

908
00:49:43,021 --> 00:49:45,107
It'll let us know you got
at least 300 feet.

909
00:49:47,359 --> 00:49:48,402
I'll do it.

910
00:49:49,945 --> 00:49:53,490
- Are you throwing in with them?
- Me? No thanks.

911
00:49:53,574 --> 00:49:56,243
I think your man there
is a little too tightly wound.

912
00:49:56,326 --> 00:49:58,412
Gonna get somebody killed.

913
00:49:58,495 --> 00:50:01,290
But I'm thinkin' we could use
that shotgun of yours.

914
00:50:01,373 --> 00:50:04,042
I saw where you parked
when I pulled in.

915
00:50:04,126 --> 00:50:06,253
Red pickup, right?
Far entrance?

916
00:50:06,336 --> 00:50:09,089
Son, you got brass balls.

917
00:50:09,173 --> 00:50:11,091
The shells are
in the glove compartment.

918
00:50:11,175 --> 00:50:12,426
Drive it back.

919
00:50:14,595 --> 00:50:15,846
All right.

920
00:50:15,929 --> 00:50:17,598
Just see they're paying out this line.

921
00:50:17,681 --> 00:50:19,892
Line's up, I'll cut her loose,

922
00:50:19,975 --> 00:50:21,351
just so you understand.

923
00:50:21,435 --> 00:50:22,478
DAVID: Yeah.

924
00:50:30,110 --> 00:50:32,446
You sure there's no way
I can talk you out of this?

925
00:50:32,529 --> 00:50:37,826
David... there's nothing out there.
Nothing in the mist.

926
00:50:37,910 --> 00:50:39,828
What if you're wrong?

927
00:50:40,913 --> 00:50:42,414
Then, I guess...

928
00:50:44,458 --> 00:50:47,461
the joke would be on me after all.

929
00:50:52,799 --> 00:50:54,009
We're gonna send back help.

930
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:57,471
You'll die out there.
All of you.

931
00:51:10,234 --> 00:51:13,445
Hey, crazy lady,
I believe in God too.

932
00:51:13,529 --> 00:51:17,491
I just don't think He's the bloodthirsty asshole
you make Him out to be.

933
00:51:17,574 --> 00:51:20,202
Well, you take that up with the devil
when you run into him.

934
00:51:20,285 --> 00:51:21,912
You just chat it over at your leisure.

935
00:51:30,587 --> 00:51:32,548
Well, let's strike out
toward the center of town.

936
00:51:51,733 --> 00:51:52,985
Keep it loose.

937
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:10,294
DAVID: Nice and easy.

938
00:52:10,377 --> 00:52:11,628
OLLIE: ( low ) Keep going.

939
00:52:14,172 --> 00:52:15,632
( Onlookers murmur )

940
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:30,272
JIM: Look.

941
00:52:33,442 --> 00:52:34,735
It's going.

942
00:52:36,778 --> 00:52:37,946
They're doing good.

943
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:41,575
Aah! Aaahhhh!

944
00:52:41,658 --> 00:52:43,827
( Onlookers screaming )

945
00:52:49,708 --> 00:52:51,168
( Cord whistles sharply )

946
00:52:56,048 --> 00:52:57,257
MAN: Put it down!

947
00:52:58,300 --> 00:53:00,594
Ohh! Pull!

948
00:53:02,471 --> 00:53:04,890
MAN: Oh, my God!
I'm slippin'!

949
00:53:06,391 --> 00:53:08,727
Pull! Back up! Back up!
Back up!

950
00:53:19,613 --> 00:53:22,032
( Onlookers scream and shout )

951
00:53:22,115 --> 00:53:23,158
Get it off!

952
00:53:32,542 --> 00:53:33,585
Oh, my God.

953
00:53:38,507 --> 00:53:40,175
( Woman sobbing )

954
00:53:40,258 --> 00:53:41,718
- JIM: Aw, sh--
- MRS. CARMODY: Blood!

955
00:53:41,802 --> 00:53:43,512
Awww, sh--!

956
00:53:43,595 --> 00:53:45,263
MRS. CARMODY:
Oh, my God!

957
00:53:46,473 --> 00:53:48,767
- ( Onlookers shouting )
- Oh, my God!

958
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:58,026
( Onlookers screaming )

959
00:54:03,281 --> 00:54:04,574
Cut the rope!

960
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:08,286
Shut the door!

961
00:54:14,042 --> 00:54:16,044
Now do you see?

962
00:54:18,046 --> 00:54:19,548
Now do you believe?

963
00:54:29,057 --> 00:54:30,892
OLLIE:
About a half-hour of daylight left.

964
00:54:32,227 --> 00:54:34,062
Guys, how's it going
with these work lights?

965
00:54:34,146 --> 00:54:37,691
- We're gettin' 'em rigged up all right.
- Yeah, check it out.

966
00:54:37,774 --> 00:54:39,693
All right, all right.
Save it, save it.

967
00:54:40,694 --> 00:54:42,237
These batteries ain't topped up.

968
00:54:42,320 --> 00:54:44,406
You turn the lights on,
it's gonna drain 'em quick.

969
00:54:44,489 --> 00:54:45,615
How quick?

970
00:54:45,699 --> 00:54:47,659
- Five minutes, maybe ten.
- Yeah, if that.

971
00:54:47,743 --> 00:54:49,745
Okay, emergencies only.

972
00:54:50,746 --> 00:54:52,247
If something gets in the store.

973
00:55:00,005 --> 00:55:02,549
( Sighs ) Holy Jesus,
you scared the shit outta me.

974
00:55:02,632 --> 00:55:04,176
Oh, Sally, I'm sorry, really.

975
00:55:05,719 --> 00:55:08,555
I thought I'd come in and say hi
and see how you were holding up.

976
00:55:08,638 --> 00:55:10,098
- Hi.
- Hi.

977
00:55:11,224 --> 00:55:12,517
Barely. How about you?

978
00:55:12,601 --> 00:55:14,186
I'm worried about my folks, I guess.

979
00:55:14,269 --> 00:55:16,938
You know, they live
up on Shorm Road.

980
00:55:17,022 --> 00:55:19,107
That's less than
five miles from here.

981
00:55:19,191 --> 00:55:20,734
How 'bout yours?

982
00:55:20,817 --> 00:55:22,402
Well, they're out of town right now.

983
00:55:23,403 --> 00:55:25,989
They're at my aunt's in Boston, so...

984
00:55:26,072 --> 00:55:28,825
That's lucky.
That means they're okay.

985
00:55:28,909 --> 00:55:30,160
I hope so.

986
00:55:32,370 --> 00:55:35,999
So... how soon you shipping out?

987
00:55:36,082 --> 00:55:37,751
Uh, couple weeks.

988
00:55:39,419 --> 00:55:40,921
Scared about going over there?

989
00:55:42,297 --> 00:55:43,340
( Softly ) Yeah.

990
00:55:48,595 --> 00:55:50,138
- Hey, Wayne?
- Hmm?

991
00:55:51,264 --> 00:55:53,308
How come you never asked me out?

992
00:55:53,391 --> 00:55:56,269
We flirted all through high school.
I know you like me.

993
00:55:56,353 --> 00:55:57,479
( Chuckles )

994
00:56:00,565 --> 00:56:02,108
So how come?

995
00:56:04,528 --> 00:56:06,363
I'm stupid, I guess.

996
00:56:22,879 --> 00:56:25,090
Oh, shit! I'm sorry.

997
00:56:25,173 --> 00:56:29,469
Don't be. I just-- I just didn't really want it
to happen like this, you know?

998
00:56:29,553 --> 00:56:32,222
Some shitty locker room at work.

999
00:56:32,305 --> 00:56:34,474
Can we just stay in here a while, then?

1000
00:56:35,892 --> 00:56:38,270
I mean, just-- just you and me.

1001
00:56:49,573 --> 00:56:53,243
- DAN:The parking lot lamps turned on.
- OLLIE:They're on a timer.

1002
00:56:53,326 --> 00:56:55,287
Must be a different municipal line.

1003
00:56:55,370 --> 00:56:58,081
DAN: Maybe we could
tie into them somehow,

1004
00:56:58,164 --> 00:57:00,041
get some electricity in here.

1005
00:57:01,042 --> 00:57:02,711
That'd mean walking out the door.

1006
00:57:13,722 --> 00:57:15,473
- Gaaaahhhh! God!
- ( woman screams )

1007
00:57:16,349 --> 00:57:17,767
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

1008
00:57:17,851 --> 00:57:19,853
- OLLIE: David! David!
- ( Indistinct )

1009
00:57:22,147 --> 00:57:23,189
WOMAN: ...you sure?

1010
00:57:23,273 --> 00:57:24,316
Look!

1011
00:57:47,422 --> 00:57:48,882
My God.

1012
00:58:03,939 --> 00:58:05,899
Are those bugs?

1013
00:58:08,109 --> 00:58:10,236
Not like any I've ever seen.

1014
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:12,447
MRS. CARMODY:
"They came out of the smoke,

1015
00:58:12,530 --> 00:58:14,449
"locusts upon the earth,

1016
00:58:14,532 --> 00:58:17,035
"and unto them was given power

1017
00:58:17,118 --> 00:58:21,289
even as the scorpions
of the earth have power."

1018
00:58:21,373 --> 00:58:23,875
( Gasps ) Wow.

1019
00:58:23,959 --> 00:58:26,419
Look at those stingers.

1020
00:58:29,881 --> 00:58:31,883
Dear God.

1021
00:58:31,883 --> 00:59:01,883
<b>Subtitle | www.movieddl.me</b>

1022
00:59:11,047 --> 00:59:12,549
Holy shit!

1023
00:59:12,632 --> 00:59:15,468
( Monster shrieks; onlookers scream )

1024
00:59:22,600 --> 00:59:24,644
( Screaming )

1025
00:59:27,981 --> 00:59:29,941
Myron, get the ones in the back!

1026
00:59:31,484 --> 00:59:33,194
God, I think they're attracted to the light.

1027
00:59:33,278 --> 00:59:35,613
- ( Screaming )
- OLLIE: Look out, look out, look out!

1028
00:59:35,697 --> 00:59:36,740
The light! Douse the light!

1029
00:59:38,450 --> 00:59:39,784
Look out! Look out!

1030
00:59:41,536 --> 00:59:44,497
( Screams and weeping )

1031
00:59:44,581 --> 00:59:45,832
Move! Move!

1032
00:59:47,834 --> 00:59:50,295
DAVID: Light, light,
light, light, light!

1033
00:59:50,378 --> 00:59:51,421
( Glass crashes )

1034
00:59:51,504 --> 00:59:53,298
"And there came a voice
from the temple

1035
00:59:53,381 --> 00:59:55,175
"saying to the seven angels,

1036
00:59:55,258 --> 00:59:57,594
" 'Go your ways

1037
00:59:57,677 --> 01:00:01,848
and pour out the vials
of the wrath of God upon the earth.' "

1038
01:00:01,931 --> 01:00:04,267
( monsters shrieking )

1039
01:00:10,732 --> 01:00:13,234
DAVID: Ollie, the glass is gonna give!

1040
01:00:21,034 --> 01:00:23,661
- DAVID: Shit!
- OLLIE: Oh, my God, they turned on all the lights!

1041
01:00:23,745 --> 01:00:25,205
- OLLIE: Jim! Myron!
- DAVID: Fire!

1042
01:00:25,288 --> 01:00:27,207
- OLLIE: Douse the lights!
- DAVID:Fire! Lighter!

1043
01:00:27,290 --> 01:00:29,542
- Come on, come on!
- ( lighter flicks )

1044
01:00:31,336 --> 01:00:32,629
Aah!

1045
01:00:32,712 --> 01:00:33,755
Whoa!

1046
01:00:35,256 --> 01:00:36,341
Aah!

1047
01:00:37,675 --> 01:00:39,511
Oh, ugh!

1048
01:00:41,054 --> 01:00:42,555
Sally, look out!

1049
01:00:44,891 --> 01:00:45,934
No!

1050
01:00:46,017 --> 01:00:48,353
Ohh! Oohhhh!

1051
01:00:48,436 --> 01:00:50,271
( Groaning )

1052
01:00:53,817 --> 01:00:56,319
Let me see, let me see.
Let me see, sweetheart, let me see.

1053
01:00:56,402 --> 01:00:58,363
No, you're gonna be okay.
You're gonna be okay.

1054
01:00:58,446 --> 01:00:59,489
Let me see. Let me see.

1055
01:00:59,572 --> 01:01:01,199
You're fine. You're gonna be okay.
You're gonna be okay.

1056
01:01:01,282 --> 01:01:02,534
Give me the lighter!
Put it on fire!

1057
01:01:02,617 --> 01:01:03,660
Come on!

1058
01:01:06,955 --> 01:01:10,125
Come on, come on!
Breathe, breathe, breathe, Sally!

1059
01:01:10,208 --> 01:01:12,794
Goddamn childproofing sons of bitches!

1060
01:01:13,795 --> 01:01:14,838
Aaahhhh!

1061
01:01:14,921 --> 01:01:17,132
AMANDA: Oh, shoot it! Shoot it!

1062
01:01:18,758 --> 01:01:20,468
Shoot it! Shoot it!

1063
01:01:20,552 --> 01:01:22,137
I can't! I'll smash the window!

1064
01:01:22,220 --> 01:01:24,389
AMANDA: ( screaming ) God!

1065
01:01:24,472 --> 01:01:26,099
Oh, God! Ohh!

1066
01:01:27,600 --> 01:01:29,352
- Aaahhh!
- Go! Go!

1067
01:01:29,435 --> 01:01:31,646
( Screams and shouts )

1068
01:01:31,729 --> 01:01:33,565
OLLIE: Get down!

1069
01:01:33,648 --> 01:01:36,442
( Screaming and shouting )

1070
01:01:39,904 --> 01:01:41,406
OLLIE: Shit!

1071
01:01:51,124 --> 01:01:52,959
- Ollie, you want these lights on or off?
- Leave 'em on.

1072
01:01:53,042 --> 01:01:55,170
( Screaming and shouting )

1073
01:01:57,046 --> 01:01:59,299
Aah! Aaahhhh!

1074
01:01:59,382 --> 01:02:00,425
Oh, God!

1075
01:02:00,508 --> 01:02:02,802
Ohh! Ohhh! Kill it!

1076
01:02:02,886 --> 01:02:05,471
Aaaaahhhhhh!

1077
01:02:05,555 --> 01:02:07,682
( Crunching )

1078
01:02:10,226 --> 01:02:11,895
( Gasping )

1079
01:02:11,978 --> 01:02:13,855
MAN:Bring torches!
Bring something to keep 'em out!

1080
01:02:13,938 --> 01:02:14,981
Come on.

1081
01:02:15,064 --> 01:02:16,858
( Sally groaning )

1082
01:02:16,941 --> 01:02:18,067
WAYNE: Sally!

1083
01:02:22,363 --> 01:02:25,992
( Screaming and shouting )

1084
01:02:29,996 --> 01:02:32,207
Where are the goddamn extinguishers?

1085
01:02:36,669 --> 01:02:38,129
WOMAN: What's happening?!

1086
01:02:39,130 --> 01:02:41,007
( Monster shrieking )

1087
01:02:42,967 --> 01:02:44,260
Get it! Get it! Get it!

1088
01:02:49,682 --> 01:02:52,644
MAN:Bring torches.
We need torches at the window!

1089
01:02:52,727 --> 01:02:54,270
Plug that hole!

1090
01:03:01,444 --> 01:03:02,487
Dad!

1091
01:03:08,409 --> 01:03:10,078
Down! Down! Lay down!

1092
01:03:19,504 --> 01:03:21,756
( Mrs. Carmody gasping )

1093
01:03:24,217 --> 01:03:25,260
Ohh.

1094
01:03:26,636 --> 01:03:27,679
My life...

1095
01:03:28,763 --> 01:03:32,183
my life for You,
Your will be done.

1096
01:03:37,939 --> 01:03:39,941
( Nervous titter )

1097
01:03:45,530 --> 01:03:47,657
- ( Screams and shouts )
- Daddy!

1098
01:03:47,740 --> 01:03:50,034
Bugs! Daddy!

1099
01:04:00,628 --> 01:04:01,671
( Gunshot )

1100
01:04:01,754 --> 01:04:03,047
( Onlookers scream )

1101
01:04:03,131 --> 01:04:05,216
( Monster shrieks )

1102
01:04:05,300 --> 01:04:07,719
- Nooooo! Billy!
- Daddy!

1103
01:04:07,802 --> 01:04:09,762
- Billy!
- Daddy!

1104
01:04:15,977 --> 01:04:18,938
( Monster shrieking )

1105
01:04:22,775 --> 01:04:24,277
HATTIE: Billy! Oh!

1106
01:04:24,360 --> 01:04:25,486
Dad!

1107
01:04:25,570 --> 01:04:27,071
HATTIE: Billy, come back here.

1108
01:04:28,781 --> 01:04:30,783
- Dad!
- Billy, please!

1109
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:32,285
( Monster shrieks )

1110
01:04:36,706 --> 01:04:37,999
HATTIE: Billy!

1111
01:04:41,127 --> 01:04:42,420
( Gunshot )

1112
01:04:42,503 --> 01:04:44,464
( Onlookers scream and shout )

1113
01:04:44,547 --> 01:04:47,592
( David panting )

1114
01:05:06,944 --> 01:05:08,237
MAN: Come on, let's move it!

1115
01:05:08,321 --> 01:05:10,281
MAN #2: Somebody please
come over here and help.

1116
01:05:10,365 --> 01:05:12,033
- ( Injured man screaming )
- MAN #3: Here's some tape!

1117
01:05:14,369 --> 01:05:16,496
MAN #4:I'm right here.
I'm right here. Don't worry.

1118
01:05:17,538 --> 01:05:19,457
MAN #5: Hurry up with the blankets!

1119
01:05:19,540 --> 01:05:22,543
INJURED MAN:
It hurts so bad! Please!

1120
01:05:30,385 --> 01:05:31,928
INJURED MAN:
It hurts so bad!

1121
01:05:32,011 --> 01:05:33,888
MAN: Block it up here.

1122
01:05:33,971 --> 01:05:36,057
Get me some more bags!

1123
01:05:37,058 --> 01:05:39,727
DAVID: Did we get 'em?
Did we get 'em all?

1124
01:05:40,728 --> 01:05:42,438
WOMAN: She was right.

1125
01:05:42,522 --> 01:05:44,816
She said that it would happen like this.

1126
01:05:44,899 --> 01:05:46,901
She said that
they would come at night.

1127
01:05:48,069 --> 01:05:49,904
She told us someone would die.

1128
01:06:02,375 --> 01:06:04,377
( Monster snarling )

1129
01:06:07,922 --> 01:06:10,716
( Monster grunting and chewing )

1130
01:06:13,928 --> 01:06:15,638
( Grunts ) Mommy.

1131
01:06:17,223 --> 01:06:19,225
Ohh, shh, shh, shh.
It's okay.

1132
01:06:20,351 --> 01:06:21,978
It's okay, it was just a dream.

1133
01:06:22,979 --> 01:06:24,355
It's just a bad dream.

1134
01:06:25,398 --> 01:06:27,150
BILLY: I want my mommy.

1135
01:06:27,233 --> 01:06:28,818
I know.

1136
01:06:28,901 --> 01:06:31,154
I know. Of course you do.

1137
01:06:31,237 --> 01:06:33,781
- Shh.
- BILLY: I wanna go home.

1138
01:06:33,865 --> 01:06:35,366
Just sleep.

1139
01:06:36,742 --> 01:06:38,411
Everything'll be better in the morning.

1140
01:06:45,084 --> 01:06:46,586
Think he likes you.

1141
01:06:49,130 --> 01:06:51,716
( low ) Well, I hate that
I had to lie to him.

1142
01:06:52,758 --> 01:06:54,218
You have kids?

1143
01:06:54,302 --> 01:06:55,553
No.

1144
01:06:55,636 --> 01:06:57,763
I always wanted to, but...

1145
01:06:58,848 --> 01:07:00,516
things haven't been working out.

1146
01:07:02,852 --> 01:07:05,855
Right now I'm thinking
maybe that's for the best.

1147
01:07:07,023 --> 01:07:10,776
I saw creatures
fly into the store tonight that--

1148
01:07:10,860 --> 01:07:12,570
They shouldn't exist.

1149
01:07:14,030 --> 01:07:16,616
I keep thinking I'm gonna
wake up in a rubber room.

1150
01:07:18,034 --> 01:07:19,285
You're not alone in that.

1151
01:07:20,328 --> 01:07:21,787
We're all right there with you.

1152
01:07:22,914 --> 01:07:24,665
This isn't gonna end, is it?

1153
01:07:27,668 --> 01:07:28,711
OLLIE: David.

1154
01:07:29,754 --> 01:07:32,006
It's Joe. He's getting worse.

1155
01:07:49,899 --> 01:07:51,859
( Sighs ) Joe.

1156
01:07:53,736 --> 01:07:55,488
How you holdin' up, partner?

1157
01:07:55,571 --> 01:07:58,908
JOE: ( labored )
David... is that you?

1158
01:08:00,034 --> 01:08:01,536
Yeah, pal, how you doin'?

1159
01:08:02,537 --> 01:08:05,289
( low ) It's bad. He's bad.

1160
01:08:05,373 --> 01:08:08,000
Didn't know anything
could hurt like this.

1161
01:08:09,001 --> 01:08:11,337
If you guys can't help me...

1162
01:08:12,547 --> 01:08:14,840
you-- you gotta end it, okay?

1163
01:08:17,051 --> 01:08:19,387
Ollie's got that gun, right?

1164
01:08:20,888 --> 01:08:23,432
- JOE: Right?
- No. No way.

1165
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:25,810
JOE: You can't fuck with me on this, bro.

1166
01:08:25,893 --> 01:08:28,062
Not with me like this.

1167
01:08:28,145 --> 01:08:29,605
I'll do it.

1168
01:08:29,689 --> 01:08:32,441
( Crying ) Just give me the gun.

1169
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:34,151
DAVID: Hey, hey. Shh.

1170
01:08:34,235 --> 01:08:37,321
- We're not there yet, okay?
- Oh, please!

1171
01:08:37,405 --> 01:08:39,156
Joe, now, listen.

1172
01:08:40,199 --> 01:08:43,369
Pal... we're gonna work something out.

1173
01:08:43,452 --> 01:08:46,289
I just need you to hang in
a little longer, okay? Can we do that?

1174
01:08:46,372 --> 01:08:48,374
( Joe weeps softly )

1175
01:08:50,209 --> 01:08:51,919
DAVID: Stay with him.
I'll be back.

1176
01:08:55,214 --> 01:08:59,218
Hattie, I need to go to the bathroom.
Will you watch Billy?

1177
01:09:01,137 --> 01:09:02,179
Hattie.

1178
01:09:18,821 --> 01:09:20,072
See anything?

1179
01:09:21,282 --> 01:09:24,201
DAN: The last of those bugs
went away about four.

1180
01:09:24,285 --> 01:09:27,455
Dawn's coming.
What's on your mind?

1181
01:09:27,538 --> 01:09:28,789
DAVID: It's Joe.

1182
01:09:30,499 --> 01:09:33,628
We don't get him on some serious antibiotics,
he's gonna die of infection.

1183
01:09:33,711 --> 01:09:36,005
OLLIE: Plus he needs
painkillers in the worst way.

1184
01:09:36,088 --> 01:09:39,884
All-- all-- all we got here
is liquor and aspirin.

1185
01:09:39,967 --> 01:09:42,720
You-- you thinkin' about goin'
to that pharmacy next door?

1186
01:09:42,803 --> 01:09:44,722
Irene Reppler says
they've got Silvadene--

1187
01:09:44,805 --> 01:09:46,599
You know, the stuff
they use in burn wards.

1188
01:09:46,682 --> 01:09:48,809
- She knows where they keep it.
- Slow down.

1189
01:09:48,893 --> 01:09:50,561
You can't actually be thinkin' of doin' this.

1190
01:09:50,645 --> 01:09:52,563
I'm also thinkin' beyond that.

1191
01:09:52,647 --> 01:09:54,315
We have to get out of here.

1192
01:09:55,358 --> 01:09:58,778
- I mean <i>permanently.</i>
- Why? We got plenty to eat!

1193
01:09:58,861 --> 01:10:01,864
And what happens when one of those things
decides to break through this window?

1194
01:10:01,947 --> 01:10:04,700
I'm talkin' one of the big ones,
like the one that killed Norm.

1195
01:10:04,784 --> 01:10:07,703
Yeah, and that flaming torch idea
didn't work so well, did it?

1196
01:10:07,787 --> 01:10:09,830
We almost burned
the goddamn store down.

1197
01:10:12,041 --> 01:10:13,626
( Soft footsteps approaching )

1198
01:10:16,087 --> 01:10:17,421
It's Hattie.

1199
01:10:21,384 --> 01:10:24,095
( Moving quietly )

1200
01:10:24,178 --> 01:10:25,262
DAVID: Here?

1201
01:10:25,346 --> 01:10:27,348
DAN: All right,
gently, now. Gently.

1202
01:10:27,431 --> 01:10:29,725
BUD: One... two... three.

1203
01:10:39,276 --> 01:10:41,529
AMANDA: I don't know
how long she was there like that,

1204
01:10:41,612 --> 01:10:42,905
lying there next to us.

1205
01:10:42,988 --> 01:10:44,657
I thought she was sleeping.

1206
01:10:46,075 --> 01:10:47,868
I got my four-wheel drive.

1207
01:10:47,952 --> 01:10:49,537
It's out there.

1208
01:10:49,620 --> 01:10:51,288
Y-you're talking about leaving?

1209
01:10:52,623 --> 01:10:54,125
Well, we...

1210
01:10:54,208 --> 01:10:56,043
should hit the pharmacy first.

1211
01:10:56,127 --> 01:10:57,586
We gotta bring back
supplies for the injured.

1212
01:10:57,670 --> 01:10:58,963
I mean, if we don't,

1213
01:10:59,046 --> 01:11:01,799
Joe Eagleton's gonna die,
and we can't let that happen.

1214
01:11:01,882 --> 01:11:03,050
But after that...

1215
01:11:04,051 --> 01:11:05,720
look, my Land Cruiser
can hold eight people.

1216
01:11:05,803 --> 01:11:08,055
I say we drive south
as far as the fuel takes us

1217
01:11:08,139 --> 01:11:10,307
and try to get clear of this mist.

1218
01:11:10,391 --> 01:11:12,435
DAN: That's it?

1219
01:11:12,518 --> 01:11:13,811
That's the plan?

1220
01:11:13,894 --> 01:11:15,855
- That's what I got.
- No, you can't mean it.

1221
01:11:15,938 --> 01:11:17,940
Not after what happened
to Norton and his group.

1222
01:11:18,023 --> 01:11:20,401
No, no, no. Amanda, <i>think.</i>

1223
01:11:20,484 --> 01:11:22,445
Norton got over 200 feet
from this store.

1224
01:11:22,528 --> 01:11:23,988
That's how much rope played out.

1225
01:11:24,071 --> 01:11:26,615
I'm parked half that distance from here.

1226
01:11:26,699 --> 01:11:28,659
But who knows how far
this mist has spread?

1227
01:11:28,743 --> 01:11:30,244
It could be the entire eastern seaboard.

1228
01:11:30,327 --> 01:11:32,496
Yeah, it could be the whole world,
for all we know.

1229
01:11:32,580 --> 01:11:35,833
Wouldn't make us any less dead,
now, would it?

1230
01:11:35,916 --> 01:11:37,793
DAN: We have one gun.

1231
01:11:37,877 --> 01:11:39,837
- How many rounds?
- OLLIE: We got ten left.

1232
01:11:39,920 --> 01:11:41,046
Ten rounds. Jesus.

1233
01:11:41,130 --> 01:11:42,757
Okay, so ten.

1234
01:11:43,758 --> 01:11:45,760
Want another reason
to get the hell out of here?

1235
01:11:45,843 --> 01:11:48,804
I'll give you the best one. Her.

1236
01:11:49,930 --> 01:11:51,432
Mrs. Carmody.

1237
01:11:51,515 --> 01:11:54,351
She's our very own Jim Jones.

1238
01:11:54,435 --> 01:11:57,104
I'd like to leave before people
start drinking the Kool-Aid.

1239
01:11:57,188 --> 01:11:58,230
He's right.

1240
01:11:58,314 --> 01:12:00,566
Flakier people get,
the better she's gonna look.

1241
01:12:00,649 --> 01:12:03,319
No, I don't buy that.
It's obvious she's nuts.

1242
01:12:03,402 --> 01:12:04,862
Look, a few people maybe, but--

1243
01:12:04,945 --> 01:12:07,239
No, I count four.
She's preachin' to 'em right now.

1244
01:12:07,323 --> 01:12:08,824
By noon, she'll have four more.

1245
01:12:08,908 --> 01:12:11,035
By tomorrow night,
when those things come back,

1246
01:12:11,118 --> 01:12:12,620
she'll have a congregation,

1247
01:12:12,703 --> 01:12:16,207
and then we can start worryin'
about who she's gonna sacrifice

1248
01:12:16,290 --> 01:12:17,917
to make it all better.

1249
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:19,668
Hmm?

1250
01:12:19,752 --> 01:12:21,670
You, Amanda?

1251
01:12:21,754 --> 01:12:23,047
My little boy?

1252
01:12:23,130 --> 01:12:24,673
DAN: He's right.

1253
01:12:24,757 --> 01:12:26,926
You don't have much faith
in humanity, do you?

1254
01:12:27,927 --> 01:12:29,345
None whatsoever.

1255
01:12:29,428 --> 01:12:30,888
I can't accept that.

1256
01:12:30,971 --> 01:12:33,682
People are basically good, decent.

1257
01:12:33,766 --> 01:12:35,851
My God, David, we're a civilized society.

1258
01:12:35,935 --> 01:12:38,938
Sure, as long as the machines
are workin' and you can dial 9-1-1,

1259
01:12:39,021 --> 01:12:41,816
but you take those things away,
you throw people in the dark,

1260
01:12:41,899 --> 01:12:43,859
you scare the <i>shit</i> out of them,

1261
01:12:43,943 --> 01:12:45,778
no more <i>rules,</i>

1262
01:12:45,861 --> 01:12:47,822
you'll see how primitive they get.

1263
01:12:47,905 --> 01:12:53,160
You scare people badly enough,
you can get 'em to do anything.

1264
01:12:53,244 --> 01:12:56,831
They'll turn to whoever
promises a solution,

1265
01:12:56,914 --> 01:12:58,123
or <i>whatever.</i>

1266
01:12:58,207 --> 01:13:00,209
Ollie, please, back me up here.

1267
01:13:00,292 --> 01:13:02,002
OLLIE: I wish I could.

1268
01:13:02,086 --> 01:13:04,380
As a species,
we're fundamentally insane.

1269
01:13:05,381 --> 01:13:10,094
Put more than two of us in a room, we pick sides
and start dreaming up reasons to kill one another.

1270
01:13:11,095 --> 01:13:13,764
Why do you think we invented
politics and religion?

1271
01:13:13,848 --> 01:13:17,560
Oh, Jesus, that's just... wrong.

1272
01:13:17,643 --> 01:13:20,145
DAVID: Look, nobody has
to decide anything now, okay?

1273
01:13:20,229 --> 01:13:23,357
First things first-- the pharmacy.

1274
01:13:24,900 --> 01:13:26,569
That'll be our test run.

1275
01:13:26,652 --> 01:13:27,695
Okay?

1276
01:13:33,242 --> 01:13:34,577
( Sighs heavily )

1277
01:13:37,913 --> 01:13:39,665
It's all right, Big Bill.

1278
01:13:39,748 --> 01:13:41,417
I'm gonna bring you back
some comic books.

1279
01:13:41,500 --> 01:13:42,835
I don't want them.

1280
01:13:42,918 --> 01:13:44,545
I want you to stay here.

1281
01:13:44,628 --> 01:13:46,630
I won't be gone long.

1282
01:13:47,756 --> 01:13:49,675
Just-- just next door.

1283
01:13:49,758 --> 01:13:51,594
Hey, you'll be safe.

1284
01:13:53,137 --> 01:13:54,179
Daddy--

1285
01:13:54,263 --> 01:13:55,764
Daddy, there are things out there.

1286
01:13:56,765 --> 01:13:58,642
Things--

1287
01:13:58,726 --> 01:14:01,645
Yeah. There's a lot
less of 'em in the daytime.

1288
01:14:03,230 --> 01:14:06,150
They'll wait. They'll wait in the mist
where you can't see 'em,

1289
01:14:06,233 --> 01:14:08,485
and then when you go
and can't get back in...

1290
01:14:08,569 --> 01:14:10,029
they'll come and eat you up!

1291
01:14:10,112 --> 01:14:12,406
- Shh.
- Daddy, don't go!

1292
01:14:12,489 --> 01:14:14,408
( Sobbing )

1293
01:14:21,749 --> 01:14:23,000
I'll be back.

1294
01:14:24,251 --> 01:14:26,837
Big Bill... I promise.

1295
01:14:26,921 --> 01:14:29,256
I'll be back, and then
I'm gonna take you home.

1296
01:14:30,257 --> 01:14:31,842
All right?

1297
01:14:31,926 --> 01:14:33,969
Together, we're going home.

1298
01:14:34,970 --> 01:14:38,265
If something happens,
anything at all, you cut and run.

1299
01:14:38,349 --> 01:14:40,976
You get your ass back in here,
for your boy's sake.

1300
01:14:41,060 --> 01:14:43,562
If something happens to me,
I want you to take care of Billy...

1301
01:14:44,605 --> 01:14:47,608
best as you can,
as long as you can.

1302
01:14:47,691 --> 01:14:49,443
Land Cruiser's yours now.

1303
01:14:50,486 --> 01:14:52,071
You-- you get him out of here.

1304
01:14:52,154 --> 01:14:53,489
You just keep drivin'.

1305
01:15:00,079 --> 01:15:02,122
Where do you think you're going,
Mr. David Drayton?

1306
01:15:02,206 --> 01:15:05,167
Are you so anxious
to make your boy an orphan?

1307
01:15:05,250 --> 01:15:07,294
My boy is no concern of yours.

1308
01:15:07,378 --> 01:15:08,671
Listen up.

1309
01:15:08,754 --> 01:15:10,714
We're going to the pharmacy.

1310
01:15:10,798 --> 01:15:12,758
We're gonna bring back some supplies.

1311
01:15:12,841 --> 01:15:16,220
Also, there may be people
trapped over there who need help.

1312
01:15:16,303 --> 01:15:18,472
- ( Onlookers murmuring )
- OLLIE: Listen, folks, listen!

1313
01:15:18,555 --> 01:15:20,516
We're not gonna take any chances.

1314
01:15:20,599 --> 01:15:22,059
If there's any trouble,

1315
01:15:22,142 --> 01:15:24,144
we'll come straight back here
to the supermarket.

1316
01:15:24,228 --> 01:15:27,564
And bring the fiends of hell
down on our heads, thank you.

1317
01:15:27,648 --> 01:15:29,108
WOMAN: She's right.

1318
01:15:29,191 --> 01:15:32,236
You'll make 'em notice us.
You'll make 'em come.

1319
01:15:33,237 --> 01:15:35,906
Why can't you just leave
well enough alone?

1320
01:15:35,990 --> 01:15:37,825
Lady, this what you call
"well enough"?

1321
01:15:37,908 --> 01:15:39,410
You wanna stop us?

1322
01:15:39,493 --> 01:15:40,995
You better explain to Bobby here

1323
01:15:41,078 --> 01:15:43,288
why we're not bringin' painkillers
and medicine back for his brother.

1324
01:15:43,372 --> 01:15:45,541
I'm goin', even if I have to go alone.

1325
01:15:45,624 --> 01:15:47,292
You'll die out there, young man.

1326
01:15:47,376 --> 01:15:50,462
You'll walk out that door
and be torn to shreds,

1327
01:15:50,546 --> 01:15:53,757
and then your hell-bound pride
will have them come get the rest of us.

1328
01:15:53,841 --> 01:15:56,635
Yes, they'll come back for all of us,
just like this good lady said.

1329
01:15:56,719 --> 01:15:58,721
Do you want that
to happen, people?

1330
01:15:58,804 --> 01:16:01,974
- ONLOOKERS: No!
- MRS. CARMODY: No! No! No!

1331
01:16:02,057 --> 01:16:04,059
Well, it is this kind of hubris

1332
01:16:04,143 --> 01:16:06,603
that brought the wrath of God
in the first place.

1333
01:16:06,687 --> 01:16:08,313
This kind of pride and defiance of--

1334
01:16:08,397 --> 01:16:10,065
( Onlookers gasp )

1335
01:16:10,149 --> 01:16:11,817
Shut up, you miserable buzzard!

1336
01:16:11,900 --> 01:16:13,152
You old bitch!

1337
01:16:13,235 --> 01:16:14,570
DAVID: No, no, no, no!

1338
01:16:17,281 --> 01:16:20,409
Stoning people who piss you off
is perfectly okay.

1339
01:16:20,492 --> 01:16:22,119
They do it in the Bible, don't they?

1340
01:16:22,202 --> 01:16:23,996
And I got lots of peas.

1341
01:16:24,079 --> 01:16:26,707
David, please, if you want to go,
now's the time.

1342
01:16:26,790 --> 01:16:28,459
How 'bout it, Army?

1343
01:16:28,542 --> 01:16:30,044
Any help from the armed forces?

1344
01:16:30,127 --> 01:16:31,170
I'll go.

1345
01:16:33,589 --> 01:16:36,633
IRENE: Jim Grondin.
I had you in school, didn't I?

1346
01:16:36,717 --> 01:16:38,677
Yes'm, me and my sister Pauline.

1347
01:16:38,761 --> 01:16:40,387
Pair of underachievers.

1348
01:16:40,471 --> 01:16:41,722
After you, Jim.

1349
01:16:42,765 --> 01:16:44,141
Yes, ma'am.

1350
01:16:44,224 --> 01:16:45,559
Oh, <i>shit.</i>

1351
01:16:45,642 --> 01:16:48,020
DAVID: That it?
That's everybody?

1352
01:16:48,103 --> 01:16:49,605
Everybody that's goin'.

1353
01:16:49,688 --> 01:16:51,732
- MAN: Yep.
- Okay.

1354
01:16:51,815 --> 01:16:54,818
DAVID: Single file,
one by one, all right?

1355
01:16:54,902 --> 01:16:56,653
Let's get this thing over with.

1356
01:16:57,821 --> 01:16:58,906
Let's go.

1357
01:16:58,989 --> 01:17:00,699
- JIM: After you.
- IRENE: Yes.

1358
01:17:03,702 --> 01:17:04,745
Stay together.

1359
01:17:04,828 --> 01:17:07,790
( Onlookers murmuring )

1360
01:17:07,873 --> 01:17:09,750
- MAN: Get the door.
- MRS. CARMODY: You know what?

1361
01:17:09,833 --> 01:17:11,335
- Mrs. Carmody, you're not helping.
- I don't care.

1362
01:17:11,418 --> 01:17:13,087
- Shut the hell up!
- You shut up!

1363
01:17:19,885 --> 01:17:21,220
DAVID: Save the batteries.

1364
01:18:08,684 --> 01:18:10,269
DAVID: ( low ) <i>Shit.</i>

1365
01:18:10,352 --> 01:18:12,354
They left the doors propped open.

1366
01:18:13,689 --> 01:18:15,232
OLLIE: ( low )
Think something got in?

1367
01:18:16,733 --> 01:18:21,238
DAVID: Let's just... get what we need,
get the hell outta here.

1368
01:18:21,321 --> 01:18:22,739
OLLIE: Yeah. Let's do that.

1369
01:18:22,823 --> 01:18:27,244
IRENE: ( low ) The meds are
over at the end there, in the cubicle.

1370
01:18:44,344 --> 01:18:45,679
( loud, sharp crash )

1371
01:18:47,723 --> 01:18:51,101
- DAVID: Will you not do that?
- JIM: ( low )I'm sorry. I'm <i>sorry.</i>

1372
01:18:51,185 --> 01:18:53,187
DAVID: ( exasperated )Oh, <i>God.</i>

1373
01:19:17,878 --> 01:19:19,171
Where's that Silvadene?

1374
01:19:19,254 --> 01:19:20,756
It's over behind David.

1375
01:19:20,839 --> 01:19:22,674
In the fridge. Check there.

1376
01:19:28,805 --> 01:19:30,265
Silvadene. Got it.

1377
01:19:30,807 --> 01:19:32,851
- Good.
- Ollie, what are we lookin' for?

1378
01:19:32,935 --> 01:19:34,436
- OLLIE: Penicillin.
- DAVID: Yeah.

1379
01:19:34,519 --> 01:19:35,979
OLLIE: ( normal volume )
Any strong antibiotics.

1380
01:19:36,063 --> 01:19:37,731
Yeah.

1381
01:19:37,814 --> 01:19:41,235
Pain meds like Vicodin or OxyContin.

1382
01:19:41,318 --> 01:19:42,819
- DAVID: Shh!
- OxyContin!

1383
01:19:44,571 --> 01:19:46,323
Hydrochloride?

1384
01:19:48,867 --> 01:19:49,910
DAVID: Penicillin.

1385
01:19:55,082 --> 01:19:56,750
( Soft scurrying sound )

1386
01:20:01,088 --> 01:20:02,130
Guys.

1387
01:20:05,968 --> 01:20:07,594
Hurry it up.
I hear something.

1388
01:20:11,473 --> 01:20:12,516
What?

1389
01:20:12,599 --> 01:20:14,685
( Soft scurrying sound )

1390
01:20:14,768 --> 01:20:16,311
DAN: Somethin' fuckin' weird.

1391
01:20:25,946 --> 01:20:27,739
Oh, God.

1392
01:20:27,948 --> 01:20:29,241
Oh, <i>God!</i>

1393
01:20:29,324 --> 01:20:33,287
No. Oh, no.

1394
01:20:33,370 --> 01:20:35,080
Oh, nooooo.

1395
01:20:35,163 --> 01:20:36,748
Oh, <i>fuck.</i>

1396
01:20:38,625 --> 01:20:40,585
IRENE: Look.
There's another one.

1397
01:20:40,669 --> 01:20:43,463
- OLLIE: Oh, my God.
- JIM: No, no, no.

1398
01:20:43,547 --> 01:20:45,882
Oh, no, no.

1399
01:20:46,508 --> 01:20:49,594
Guys, let's get out of here <i>now.</i>

1400
01:20:50,637 --> 01:20:52,556
- Aaaahhhhhh!
- OLLIE: Holy shit!

1401
01:20:52,639 --> 01:20:53,932
( Jim screaming )

1402
01:20:56,476 --> 01:20:59,146
JIM: Shit! Shit! Oh, shit!

1403
01:20:59,229 --> 01:21:03,608
M.P.:I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
Help me!

1404
01:21:03,692 --> 01:21:05,777
IRENE: Good Lord!
Help him!

1405
01:21:06,820 --> 01:21:10,032
( M.P. groaning )

1406
01:21:11,575 --> 01:21:13,076
DAVID: Son of a bitch!

1407
01:21:13,160 --> 01:21:14,703
This stuff ain't comin' off!

1408
01:21:15,787 --> 01:21:18,123
Oh, man!
He's glued to this fuckin' post!

1409
01:21:18,206 --> 01:21:20,000
( Hoarsely )
It's our fault.

1410
01:21:20,083 --> 01:21:22,169
It's all our fault.

1411
01:21:22,252 --> 01:21:23,670
DAVID: It's really stuck.

1412
01:21:24,713 --> 01:21:25,964
( Groaning )

1413
01:21:28,008 --> 01:21:30,010
M.P.: God, I can feel 'em!

1414
01:21:30,093 --> 01:21:32,137
I can feel 'em!

1415
01:21:32,220 --> 01:21:33,680
( Groaning )

1416
01:21:33,764 --> 01:21:35,724
WAYNE: Oh, my God!
<i>Jesus!</i>

1417
01:21:42,856 --> 01:21:44,483
Oh, my God.

1418
01:21:44,566 --> 01:21:47,027
Ohh! I--

1419
01:21:48,070 --> 01:21:49,529
Aaahhhh!

1420
01:21:49,613 --> 01:21:50,530
( Gasps )

1421
01:21:50,614 --> 01:21:53,075
Aah! Aaaaahhhhhh!

1422
01:21:53,158 --> 01:21:54,868
( Monster shrieks )

1423
01:21:56,370 --> 01:21:58,288
- ( Gunshot )
- There's more!

1424
01:21:58,372 --> 01:21:59,414
Ohh!

1425
01:22:03,710 --> 01:22:04,920
( Web sizzles )

1426
01:22:05,003 --> 01:22:06,838
( M.P. groans )

1427
01:22:06,922 --> 01:22:09,591
- Aah! Aah!
- DAN:There's another one! Hit it!

1428
01:22:11,468 --> 01:22:13,762
- Aah!
- OLLIE: What the hell is that stuff?

1429
01:22:13,845 --> 01:22:15,639
Ollie! One over there!

1430
01:22:15,722 --> 01:22:17,349
Ollie, there!

1431
01:22:17,432 --> 01:22:19,142
Got it!

1432
01:22:19,226 --> 01:22:21,686
There, there, there!
Shoot! Shoot!

1433
01:22:21,770 --> 01:22:23,647
- ( Monster squeals )
- Shit!

1434
01:22:23,730 --> 01:22:26,900
DAN:Where are they?
You see 'em?

1435
01:22:26,983 --> 01:22:30,028
- Where the hell are they?
- Aah! Aaaahhhhh!

1436
01:22:30,112 --> 01:22:31,238
Bobby!

1437
01:22:31,446 --> 01:22:32,948
Bobby!

1438
01:22:33,031 --> 01:22:35,283
( Monster shrieking )

1439
01:22:35,367 --> 01:22:38,078
( Bobby screaming )

1440
01:22:38,161 --> 01:22:40,622
- Aaahhhh!
- Hold on, man! Hold on!

1441
01:22:40,705 --> 01:22:42,374
- Hold on, man!
- Cut the strand!

1442
01:22:42,457 --> 01:22:43,500
- ( Gunshot )
- Help me!

1443
01:22:43,583 --> 01:22:44,751
( Gunshot )

1444
01:22:44,835 --> 01:22:46,545
IRENE: Let's get out of here!

1445
01:22:46,628 --> 01:22:48,505
( Screaming and shouting )

1446
01:22:48,588 --> 01:22:50,924
- A belt! Who's got a belt?
- I got a belt!

1447
01:22:52,551 --> 01:22:55,720
- Aaaaahhhhhh!
- Hold it tight.

1448
01:22:55,804 --> 01:22:58,432
- I got him, I got him. Hold on.
- I can't feel my--

1449
01:22:58,515 --> 01:22:59,891
DAVID: Pull it tight!

1450
01:23:01,435 --> 01:23:03,103
OLLIE: Look! Look!

1451
01:23:03,186 --> 01:23:05,772
Aaahhh! Aaaaahhhhhh!

1452
01:23:07,190 --> 01:23:08,984
Ohhhhhh!

1453
01:23:09,067 --> 01:23:10,777
Gaaahhhh!

1454
01:23:10,861 --> 01:23:12,404
DAVID: Light!

1455
01:23:12,487 --> 01:23:13,530
Light!

1456
01:23:13,613 --> 01:23:16,158
- ( Monster shrieks )
- God!

1457
01:23:19,244 --> 01:23:22,456
JIM: We gotta get outta here!
Come on!

1458
01:23:22,539 --> 01:23:24,958
WAYNE: Let's go, let's go,
let's go, let's go, let's go!

1459
01:23:25,041 --> 01:23:27,002
DAVID: Watch it, watch it, watch it!

1460
01:23:33,258 --> 01:23:34,759
( Monster shrieks )

1461
01:23:38,346 --> 01:23:40,432
DAN: Let's get out of here!

1462
01:23:40,515 --> 01:23:43,810
All right, go, go, go, go, go, go!
Come on!

1463
01:23:43,894 --> 01:23:45,020
DAVID: Come on!

1464
01:23:49,483 --> 01:23:51,234
( loud crash )

1465
01:23:52,319 --> 01:23:54,946
WAYNE: Oh, my God! We can't go.

1466
01:23:55,947 --> 01:23:57,657
Ollie! Ollie!

1467
01:24:00,535 --> 01:24:02,078
( Dry fires )

1468
01:24:02,162 --> 01:24:03,997
WAYNE: Kill it! Kill it!

1469
01:24:10,420 --> 01:24:12,797
( Grunting )

1470
01:24:14,674 --> 01:24:16,927
- Fuckers!
- Oh, no! Oh, God, he's dead!

1471
01:24:17,010 --> 01:24:19,596
He's dead! Get out of here!
Let's go, let's go!

1472
01:24:19,679 --> 01:24:22,015
Drayton, come on,
come on, come on!

1473
01:24:22,098 --> 01:24:24,142
Come on, Drayton, he's dead!
Come on!

1474
01:24:53,255 --> 01:24:55,257
( Onlookers scream )

1475
01:24:55,340 --> 01:24:56,633
JIM: Open the door!

1476
01:24:56,716 --> 01:24:58,218
( Shouting and screaming )

1477
01:24:58,301 --> 01:24:59,427
MAN: Where's Bobby?

1478
01:24:59,511 --> 01:25:00,554
Daddy!

1479
01:25:02,055 --> 01:25:03,139
MAN: Close up the doors!

1480
01:25:03,223 --> 01:25:04,266
Hurry up!

1481
01:25:04,349 --> 01:25:05,809
What happened?

1482
01:25:05,892 --> 01:25:08,603
JIM: They're dead!
They're all dead!

1483
01:25:08,687 --> 01:25:11,189
( Jim crying hysterically )

1484
01:25:14,859 --> 01:25:16,820
( Crying hysterically )

1485
01:25:19,072 --> 01:25:21,074
( Billy crying softly )

1486
01:25:25,245 --> 01:25:27,539
MRS. CARMODY:
...expiation, because we have seen

1487
01:25:27,622 --> 01:25:30,166
the earth scourged
with whips and scorpions.

1488
01:25:30,250 --> 01:25:34,254
We have seen the earth
vomit forth from her lips

1489
01:25:34,337 --> 01:25:38,717
obscenities and profanities
of such nightmare proportions.

1490
01:25:38,800 --> 01:25:42,637
And for these evil, lurking spirits,

1491
01:25:42,721 --> 01:25:44,681
and for these evil people...

1492
01:25:44,764 --> 01:25:46,099
How long was I out?

1493
01:25:46,182 --> 01:25:47,601
Most of the day.

1494
01:25:48,643 --> 01:25:51,187
You just came over here,
lay down, and went to sleep.

1495
01:25:51,271 --> 01:25:52,856
Just passed out, is more like it.

1496
01:25:52,939 --> 01:25:54,399
MRS. CARMODY:
What will stop this Great Whore?

1497
01:25:54,482 --> 01:25:57,444
Just shut down for a while. Sorry.

1498
01:25:57,527 --> 01:25:59,112
MRS. CARMODY: How will it end?

1499
01:25:59,195 --> 01:26:00,238
CROWD: Expiation!

1500
01:26:00,322 --> 01:26:02,866
MRS. CARMODY: Expiation!
Do you remember yesterday when...

1501
01:26:02,949 --> 01:26:04,618
DAVID: How's Joe?

1502
01:26:04,701 --> 01:26:08,163
Dead. Joe died of his burns
while you were asleep.

1503
01:26:08,788 --> 01:26:10,498
We were just too late.

1504
01:26:10,582 --> 01:26:14,377
- MRS. CARMODY:I <i>told</i> you this would come!
- DAVID:Oh, God, I thought I was dreaming her voice.

1505
01:26:14,461 --> 01:26:15,795
AMANDA: No dream.

1506
01:26:15,879 --> 01:26:18,048
She's getting people whipped up.

1507
01:26:18,131 --> 01:26:23,345
That poor girl is dead,
and that boy is burnt in the back room!

1508
01:26:23,428 --> 01:26:27,265
She's got 'em believing she's a psychic;
she has a direct line with God.

1509
01:26:27,349 --> 01:26:29,851
Why wouldn't they?
Woman never shuts up.

1510
01:26:29,934 --> 01:26:32,228
Like those speeches
Castro used to make.

1511
01:26:32,312 --> 01:26:34,898
( Carmody's followers applauds )

1512
01:26:34,981 --> 01:26:38,276
Ollie says you're thinking of leaving.

1513
01:26:38,360 --> 01:26:39,694
I'm in.

1514
01:26:39,778 --> 01:26:41,738
DAVID: No. Sorry.

1515
01:26:41,821 --> 01:26:45,575
I mean, come on, you saw what
happened to <i>Bobby...</i> Mike...

1516
01:26:45,659 --> 01:26:49,454
I won't... do that again.
I won't be responsible.

1517
01:26:49,537 --> 01:26:51,039
You might want to reconsider that.

1518
01:26:51,122 --> 01:26:54,417
MRS. CARMODY: What will-- what will keep
these evil, these abominations at bay?

1519
01:26:54,501 --> 01:26:56,002
What will keep them away?

1520
01:26:56,086 --> 01:26:58,963
"The rock will not hide them.
The dead tree gives no shelter."

1521
01:26:59,047 --> 01:27:00,548
What will end it?
Let me hear it.

1522
01:27:00,632 --> 01:27:02,592
- Expiation!
- So what are we talking about?

1523
01:27:02,676 --> 01:27:05,178
- Expiation!
- Yeah, say it again like you mean it!

1524
01:27:05,261 --> 01:27:06,554
Expiation!

1525
01:27:06,638 --> 01:27:11,643
Welcome to <i>Sesame Street.</i>
Today's word is "expiation."

1526
01:27:11,726 --> 01:27:13,770
Hallelujah! Hallelujah!

1527
01:27:13,853 --> 01:27:16,439
That boy hasn't been right
since the pharmacy.

1528
01:27:16,523 --> 01:27:19,526
His mind's just snapped. Gone.

1529
01:27:19,609 --> 01:27:21,194
Hasn't even been two days.

1530
01:27:22,195 --> 01:27:23,697
Not even two days.

1531
01:27:23,780 --> 01:27:26,366
CORNELL: I'm not spendin' the rest
of my life here, I'll tell you what.

1532
01:27:26,449 --> 01:27:29,119
OLLIE: I can quietly gather up
some bags of groceries

1533
01:27:29,202 --> 01:27:32,497
and hide them up at one of
the check stands by the door.

1534
01:27:32,580 --> 01:27:34,874
DAN: It was your idea.
It's your vehicle.

1535
01:27:34,958 --> 01:27:36,459
It'll be your call.

1536
01:27:38,420 --> 01:27:40,922
I'd rather die out there trying
than in here waiting.

1537
01:27:41,005 --> 01:27:42,966
( Followers applaud )

1538
01:27:43,049 --> 01:27:45,301
MRS. CARMODY:
Who will save them? No one.

1539
01:27:45,385 --> 01:27:48,471
These rocks <i>will</i> not hide them.

1540
01:27:48,555 --> 01:27:53,309
I want some idea of what we're up against.
I want to know what this mist is.

1541
01:27:54,310 --> 01:27:57,188
- I want to talk to the soldiers.
- Soldiers? What's that gonna do?

1542
01:27:57,272 --> 01:27:59,441
You heard what that M.P. said
at the pharmacy.

1543
01:27:59,524 --> 01:28:01,818
David, I'm not even sure
I knew he was talking.

1544
01:28:01,901 --> 01:28:03,570
The situation was insane.

1545
01:28:03,653 --> 01:28:05,447
He said he was sorry.

1546
01:28:05,530 --> 01:28:07,490
Wasn't that the word
he used-- "sorry"?

1547
01:28:07,574 --> 01:28:09,868
That's right.
He said it was their fault, right?

1548
01:28:09,951 --> 01:28:13,788
- AMANDA: What did he mean by that?
- That's what we're gonna find out.

1549
01:28:13,872 --> 01:28:15,498
Irene, stay with Billy, please.

1550
01:28:15,582 --> 01:28:16,916
MRS. CARMODY:
Verse 17!

1551
01:28:17,000 --> 01:28:19,461
"...poured out his vial into the air,

1552
01:28:19,544 --> 01:28:21,421
"and there came a great voice

1553
01:28:21,504 --> 01:28:24,215
"out of the temple of heaven
from the throne, saying,

1554
01:28:24,299 --> 01:28:26,801
" 'It is done! It is done!'

1555
01:28:26,885 --> 01:28:30,138
"And there were voices
and lightning,

1556
01:28:30,221 --> 01:28:33,224
and thunders,
and a great earthquake."

1557
01:28:33,308 --> 01:28:35,977
Yes! Come to me!

1558
01:28:36,060 --> 01:28:37,187
WAYNE: What?

1559
01:28:37,270 --> 01:28:39,522
- Where's your friends?
- I ain't seen 'em.

1560
01:28:39,606 --> 01:28:41,858
Not that big a store.
It's kinda hard to lose.

1561
01:28:41,941 --> 01:28:44,944
I ain't seen 'em, I said.
I look like their keeper?

1562
01:28:48,072 --> 01:28:51,034
- What do you want from me?
- What do you know about this mist?

1563
01:28:51,117 --> 01:28:53,536
I don't know nothin'.
I got nothin' to do with it.

1564
01:28:53,620 --> 01:28:57,415
That's not what the M.P. said in the pharmacy
before the spiders came out of his skin.

1565
01:28:58,833 --> 01:29:00,585
They're not in the store.

1566
01:29:00,668 --> 01:29:03,838
The only place we haven't looked
is the loading dock.

1567
01:29:03,922 --> 01:29:04,964
...because you know.

1568
01:29:05,048 --> 01:29:07,133
You saw the good face
of God tonight.

1569
01:29:07,217 --> 01:29:08,468
Yes? Tell us.

1570
01:29:08,551 --> 01:29:10,762
Here is an old man who has seen!

1571
01:29:10,845 --> 01:29:12,972
- Yes, he has <i>seen!</i>
- ( applauding )

1572
01:29:13,056 --> 01:29:14,098
MAN: Amen.

1573
01:29:14,182 --> 01:29:17,852
MRS. CARMODY:And I <i>want</i> to say,
do I want to walk with you

1574
01:29:17,936 --> 01:29:20,605
into my Father's hands?

1575
01:29:21,105 --> 01:29:22,148
Morales.

1576
01:29:23,149 --> 01:29:24,192
Donaldson.

1577
01:29:26,778 --> 01:29:27,987
Guys...

1578
01:29:30,198 --> 01:29:33,743
- It's the only place they can be.
- WAYNE: What?

1579
01:29:33,827 --> 01:29:35,245
OLLIE: Couldn't just disappear.

1580
01:29:35,328 --> 01:29:38,289
WAYNE: Look, I told you,
okay, I don't know where they are--

1581
01:29:38,373 --> 01:29:40,500
( Sharp gasp )

1582
01:29:45,380 --> 01:29:47,131
I didn't think they'd do it.

1583
01:29:47,215 --> 01:29:49,509
They said they would do it, and I just--

1584
01:29:49,592 --> 01:29:52,971
I told them what the M.P. said at the pharmacy,
and they swore they'd do it.

1585
01:29:53,054 --> 01:29:55,807
I just-- I didn't think they would. Oh, Jesus!

1586
01:29:55,890 --> 01:29:59,060
It's the Arrowhead Project, isn't it?

1587
01:29:59,143 --> 01:30:02,647
This mist, it's some kind of,
what, military fuck up?

1588
01:30:02,730 --> 01:30:04,399
What were you guys
messin' with up there, huh?

1589
01:30:04,482 --> 01:30:07,277
We got you now,
you sorry son of a bitch!

1590
01:30:07,360 --> 01:30:08,403
Get in there!

1591
01:30:08,486 --> 01:30:11,406
It was them!
It was them what done it to us!

1592
01:30:11,489 --> 01:30:14,993
It was them what brung down
the final wrath upon us!

1593
01:30:15,076 --> 01:30:17,495
Those two peckerwoods
that he's been with this whole time,

1594
01:30:17,579 --> 01:30:19,956
they hung themselves in the back
because they knew!

1595
01:30:20,039 --> 01:30:21,541
They knew it all along!

1596
01:30:21,624 --> 01:30:23,459
- He's crazy. He doesn't know--
- Get on your knees!

1597
01:30:23,543 --> 01:30:24,836
- ( Shouting )
- MAN: Stay out of it, Drayton!

1598
01:30:24,919 --> 01:30:26,963
They heard it too, didn't you?
All of ya!

1599
01:30:27,046 --> 01:30:30,466
All about the Arrowhead Project
and all that secret shit up on the mountain.

1600
01:30:30,550 --> 01:30:32,051
That's what brung it down on us.

1601
01:30:32,135 --> 01:30:34,178
That's what brung down the wrath of God!

1602
01:30:34,262 --> 01:30:35,305
MRS. CARMODY: Oh!

1603
01:30:37,098 --> 01:30:39,058
Private Jessup.

1604
01:30:40,935 --> 01:30:42,103
It wasn't me.

1605
01:30:42,186 --> 01:30:44,480
I'm just--
I'm <i>stationed</i> up there.

1606
01:30:44,564 --> 01:30:46,024
I'm not responsible--

1607
01:30:46,107 --> 01:30:47,692
- Bullshit!
- Hell, I'm a local!

1608
01:30:47,775 --> 01:30:49,819
Most of you people know me.

1609
01:30:49,903 --> 01:30:55,033
You stop your chicken shit whining
or I will cut your puling tongue out.

1610
01:30:55,116 --> 01:30:56,701
Now you tell us!

1611
01:30:56,784 --> 01:30:58,119
( Coughs )

1612
01:30:58,202 --> 01:30:59,871
MRS. CARMODY: Tell us.

1613
01:30:59,954 --> 01:31:02,624
Look, look. Okay, okay.

1614
01:31:02,707 --> 01:31:04,125
I heard stuff.

1615
01:31:04,208 --> 01:31:05,501
Stuff?

1616
01:31:05,585 --> 01:31:07,587
Yes, we all heard stuff.

1617
01:31:08,922 --> 01:31:12,675
Like how they, um...

1618
01:31:12,759 --> 01:31:14,844
how they thought
that there were other dimensions,

1619
01:31:14,928 --> 01:31:17,722
you know, other--
other worlds all around us,

1620
01:31:17,805 --> 01:31:20,308
and how they wanted
to try and make, um,

1621
01:31:20,391 --> 01:31:21,851
a window--

1622
01:31:21,935 --> 01:31:24,562
You know, so they could look through
and see what's on the other side.

1623
01:31:26,773 --> 01:31:29,484
Well, maybe your window
turned out to be a door. Didn't it?

1624
01:31:29,567 --> 01:31:31,402
Not mine! Those scientists'!

1625
01:31:31,486 --> 01:31:34,072
- Oh, the scientists!
- Yes, the scientists!

1626
01:31:34,155 --> 01:31:36,199
They must have ripped
a hole open by accident.

1627
01:31:36,282 --> 01:31:38,117
This other world
came spilling through to ours.

1628
01:31:38,201 --> 01:31:41,496
That's what Donaldson was saying
to me right before he killed himself.

1629
01:31:41,579 --> 01:31:43,581
I didn't understand the half of it.

1630
01:31:45,500 --> 01:31:47,085
It ain't my fault!

1631
01:31:47,168 --> 01:31:48,211
Oh.

1632
01:31:49,295 --> 01:31:52,632
Ain't. His. Fault.

1633
01:31:52,715 --> 01:31:55,218
- ( Angry murmuring )
- No, no, no.

1634
01:31:55,301 --> 01:31:59,305
Ain't nothin' ever anybody's fault.

1635
01:31:59,389 --> 01:32:01,724
But he denies it.

1636
01:32:01,808 --> 01:32:04,268
He points the finger,

1637
01:32:04,352 --> 01:32:07,480
this Judas in our midst.

1638
01:32:07,563 --> 01:32:08,606
CROWD: Judas!

1639
01:32:08,690 --> 01:32:10,441
David!

1640
01:32:10,525 --> 01:32:12,777
You! You!

1641
01:32:12,860 --> 01:32:14,779
Don't you know by now?

1642
01:32:14,862 --> 01:32:16,948
Don't you know the truth?

1643
01:32:17,031 --> 01:32:19,617
We are being punished.

1644
01:32:19,701 --> 01:32:23,246
For what? For going
against the will of God!

1645
01:32:23,329 --> 01:32:27,583
For going against
His forbidden rules of old!

1646
01:32:27,667 --> 01:32:29,127
Walking on the moon!

1647
01:32:29,210 --> 01:32:30,712
Yes! Yes!

1648
01:32:30,795 --> 01:32:33,673
- Or-- or splitting His atoms!
- MAN: Amen!

1649
01:32:33,756 --> 01:32:38,469
Or-- or-- or stem cells and abortions!

1650
01:32:38,553 --> 01:32:41,514
And destroying the secrets of life

1651
01:32:41,597 --> 01:32:44,851
that only God above has any right to!

1652
01:32:44,934 --> 01:32:46,436
Amen! Amen!

1653
01:32:46,519 --> 01:32:49,063
MRS. CARMODY:
Yes, I know! It is true!

1654
01:32:49,147 --> 01:32:51,733
And now we are being punished.

1655
01:32:51,816 --> 01:32:54,694
The judgment is being
brought down upon us.

1656
01:32:54,777 --> 01:32:57,447
The fiends of hell,
you see they are let loose,

1657
01:32:57,530 --> 01:33:01,159
and star Wormwood blazes!

1658
01:33:01,242 --> 01:33:02,493
And it is his fault!

1659
01:33:02,577 --> 01:33:05,955
No! No! It is not my fault! No!

1660
01:33:06,039 --> 01:33:09,000
<i>They</i> did it! They spit
in the eye of the Almighty!

1661
01:33:09,083 --> 01:33:10,126
No!

1662
01:33:10,209 --> 01:33:12,336
- ( Angry shouting )
- MACKEY:Get over there!

1663
01:33:12,879 --> 01:33:14,005
DAVID: No!

1664
01:33:14,088 --> 01:33:15,715
MACKEY: Judas!

1665
01:33:17,008 --> 01:33:18,051
OLLIE: Jim!

1666
01:33:18,134 --> 01:33:20,553
Kill him! String him up!

1667
01:33:23,598 --> 01:33:25,308
Stand up, you coward!

1668
01:33:25,391 --> 01:33:26,350
Unkh!

1669
01:33:26,434 --> 01:33:29,812
( Scattered applause )

1670
01:33:29,896 --> 01:33:31,022
Jesus!

1671
01:33:33,983 --> 01:33:35,234
DAVID: No!

1672
01:33:35,318 --> 01:33:36,694
Aaaahhhh!

1673
01:33:36,778 --> 01:33:38,905
MACKEY: Expiation!

1674
01:33:38,988 --> 01:33:40,615
- No!
- MAN: Stab him!

1675
01:33:42,158 --> 01:33:44,077
- Aaahhhh!
- Expiation!

1676
01:33:44,160 --> 01:33:46,871
Feed him to the beast!

1677
01:33:46,954 --> 01:33:48,915
Expiation!

1678
01:33:48,998 --> 01:33:52,960
Let the abominations
smell his blood!

1679
01:33:54,462 --> 01:33:56,130
No, no! No!

1680
01:33:56,214 --> 01:33:58,800
Aaaaahhhhh!

1681
01:33:58,883 --> 01:34:02,095
- Jesus! Wait!
- No, David!

1682
01:34:06,766 --> 01:34:09,352
Aaahhhh!

1683
01:34:09,435 --> 01:34:11,938
( Crowd screaming and shouting )

1684
01:34:16,567 --> 01:34:19,070
( Groans )

1685
01:34:20,238 --> 01:34:21,948
Aaahhhh!

1686
01:34:22,031 --> 01:34:25,451
( Weeping )

1687
01:34:26,494 --> 01:34:27,995
( Groaning and gasping )

1688
01:34:29,914 --> 01:34:31,374
( Door locks )

1689
01:34:31,457 --> 01:34:33,543
Aah! Aaahhh!

1690
01:34:33,626 --> 01:34:36,587
Aaahhhh!

1691
01:34:37,755 --> 01:34:39,715
Aaahhh! Aah!

1692
01:34:39,799 --> 01:34:42,135
( Monster roars )

1693
01:34:58,818 --> 01:35:00,236
Please.

1694
01:35:01,279 --> 01:35:03,239
( Onlookers scream )

1695
01:35:04,490 --> 01:35:06,284
( Distant monster roars )

1696
01:35:10,872 --> 01:35:13,541
MRS. CARMODY:
The beast will leave us alone tonight.

1697
01:35:15,001 --> 01:35:16,252
Tomorrow...

1698
01:35:17,378 --> 01:35:19,881
tomorrow, we'll just
have to wait and see.

1699
01:35:29,223 --> 01:35:30,391
BILLY: ( softly ) Daddy.

1700
01:35:32,059 --> 01:35:33,227
Daddy.

1701
01:35:45,072 --> 01:35:46,908
( Softly ) Sorry I left you, pal.

1702
01:35:49,243 --> 01:35:50,912
I'll never leave you again.

1703
01:35:52,246 --> 01:35:53,414
Promise?

1704
01:35:54,832 --> 01:35:58,544
But you have to give me
your best promise, okay?

1705
01:35:58,628 --> 01:36:02,006
Your very best promise,
and can never break it.

1706
01:36:02,089 --> 01:36:03,841
Tell me.

1707
01:36:05,551 --> 01:36:07,887
Promise you won't let
the monsters get me.

1708
01:36:11,557 --> 01:36:13,726
Ever. No matter what.

1709
01:36:15,394 --> 01:36:16,896
I promise.

1710
01:36:20,107 --> 01:36:21,943
I love you, Daddy.

1711
01:36:22,026 --> 01:36:23,903
I love you, Billy.

1712
01:36:24,904 --> 01:36:26,239
More than anything.

1713
01:36:55,935 --> 01:36:57,103
( Softly ) It's dawn.

1714
01:37:02,525 --> 01:37:05,361
Hey, pal, you ready to go home?

1715
01:37:05,444 --> 01:37:06,779
Come on.

1716
01:37:09,198 --> 01:37:12,201
Okay, I got the groceries
hidden at check stand number two.

1717
01:37:12,285 --> 01:37:14,829
Five bags. We can grab 'em
and get out the door.

1718
01:37:14,912 --> 01:37:16,163
Okay.

1719
01:37:16,247 --> 01:37:19,959
My car's parked in the center lane
of the parking lot, far end.

1720
01:37:20,042 --> 01:37:22,253
Whoever gets there first,
open up both doors,

1721
01:37:22,336 --> 01:37:24,964
and we'll all pile in
as fast as we can, okay?

1722
01:37:25,047 --> 01:37:26,173
Let's go.

1723
01:37:49,572 --> 01:37:51,782
Stealing food now?

1724
01:37:56,037 --> 01:37:58,039
Going out now, Mrs. Carmody.

1725
01:37:59,373 --> 01:38:01,000
Please stand aside.

1726
01:38:02,418 --> 01:38:05,004
You can't go out.
I won't allow it.

1727
01:38:05,087 --> 01:38:06,380
Won't allow it?

1728
01:38:06,464 --> 01:38:09,091
It's against God's will.

1729
01:38:09,175 --> 01:38:11,344
Don't you know that by now?

1730
01:38:11,427 --> 01:38:15,931
Haven't I proven myself
again and again and again?

1731
01:38:16,015 --> 01:38:20,478
Haven't I shown that I am His vessel?

1732
01:38:25,358 --> 01:38:26,859
What's the matter with you?

1733
01:38:30,196 --> 01:38:31,655
Don't you believe in God?

1734
01:38:32,656 --> 01:38:34,241
No one's interfered with you.

1735
01:38:34,325 --> 01:38:36,911
All we're asking for
is the same privilege.

1736
01:38:36,994 --> 01:38:38,287
You heard him.

1737
01:38:39,872 --> 01:38:43,876
It is these people
who brought this upon us.

1738
01:38:45,086 --> 01:38:50,132
They-- people who refused
to bend to the will of God,

1739
01:38:50,216 --> 01:38:52,802
and claim it privilege.

1740
01:38:52,885 --> 01:38:55,888
Sinners in pride.

1741
01:38:55,971 --> 01:38:57,973
Yes, haughty.

1742
01:38:58,057 --> 01:39:00,142
Privileged!

1743
01:39:00,226 --> 01:39:04,021
They mock us. They mock our--
our God, our faith,

1744
01:39:04,105 --> 01:39:07,525
our values, our very lifestyle.

1745
01:39:07,608 --> 01:39:09,819
They mock our humility

1746
01:39:09,902 --> 01:39:11,821
and our piousness.

1747
01:39:11,904 --> 01:39:14,907
They piss on us and laugh.

1748
01:39:18,160 --> 01:39:23,416
It's from them the blood
of human sacrifice must come.

1749
01:39:23,499 --> 01:39:25,459
From them...

1750
01:39:25,543 --> 01:39:28,129
- Come on.
- ...the blood of expiation.

1751
01:39:28,212 --> 01:39:29,255
JIM: Come on.

1752
01:39:29,338 --> 01:39:30,798
You try it.

1753
01:39:30,881 --> 01:39:32,216
Fuckin' try it!

1754
01:39:32,299 --> 01:39:33,759
Come on!

1755
01:39:33,843 --> 01:39:36,053
- MAN: Get 'em!
- We want the boy.

1756
01:39:36,137 --> 01:39:37,513
- We want the boy!
- You get back!

1757
01:39:37,596 --> 01:39:39,682
- Yeah!
- You get back!

1758
01:39:39,765 --> 01:39:40,683
The boy!

1759
01:39:40,766 --> 01:39:42,184
David! David!

1760
01:39:42,268 --> 01:39:44,103
Grab that boy! Grab him!

1761
01:39:44,186 --> 01:39:46,522
- Get off me!
- ( followers shouting )

1762
01:39:46,605 --> 01:39:48,065
Get off me! Get off me!

1763
01:39:48,149 --> 01:39:49,483
Grab him!

1764
01:39:51,110 --> 01:39:52,945
And get the whore too!

1765
01:39:53,028 --> 01:39:54,488
Grab her!

1766
01:39:54,572 --> 01:39:56,949
Kill 'em! Kill 'em all!

1767
01:39:57,032 --> 01:39:58,534
( Gunshot )

1768
01:39:58,617 --> 01:40:00,286
( Onlookers gasp and fall silent )

1769
01:40:08,627 --> 01:40:10,880
( Onlookers scream )

1770
01:40:12,006 --> 01:40:13,674
MAN: Stay down!
Stay down! Stay down!

1771
01:40:13,757 --> 01:40:14,800
( Debris clanks )

1772
01:40:20,764 --> 01:40:22,433
I-- I killed her.

1773
01:40:24,560 --> 01:40:25,811
Thank you, Ollie.

1774
01:40:27,771 --> 01:40:29,023
Let's go.

1775
01:40:30,107 --> 01:40:33,319
Get that ice machine
out of the way, please.

1776
01:40:35,821 --> 01:40:37,490
WOMAN: You killed her!

1777
01:40:37,573 --> 01:40:39,867
You <i>murdered</i> her!

1778
01:40:43,454 --> 01:40:46,665
I wouldn't have shot her, Dave,
not if there'd been any other way.

1779
01:40:46,749 --> 01:40:48,209
That's why I said thank you.

1780
01:40:48,292 --> 01:40:49,460
Okay.

1781
01:40:49,543 --> 01:40:51,837
Okay, then... let's go!

1782
01:40:51,921 --> 01:40:54,840
- ( Sharp thud )
- Get up, Myron!

1783
01:40:54,924 --> 01:40:57,259
- Come on! We gotta go!
- My ankle!

1784
01:40:57,343 --> 01:40:59,803
( Women sobbing softly )

1785
01:41:05,643 --> 01:41:09,897
Okay. All the way down!
Where are they?

1786
01:41:09,980 --> 01:41:12,399
Bud! Myron!

1787
01:41:12,483 --> 01:41:13,526
Ambrose!

1788
01:41:13,609 --> 01:41:15,194
I think I broke it!

1789
01:41:15,277 --> 01:41:16,820
Come on! Come on!

1790
01:41:16,904 --> 01:41:18,364
AMANDA: We gotta go!
Come on, come on!

1791
01:41:18,447 --> 01:41:19,698
IRENE: They're lost!

1792
01:41:21,242 --> 01:41:23,202
( Amanda gasping )

1793
01:41:27,414 --> 01:41:28,999
- Oh, Jesus.
- Ollie!

1794
01:41:29,083 --> 01:41:31,669
- Ollie!
- ( monster roars )

1795
01:41:31,752 --> 01:41:33,712
Aaahhhh!

1796
01:41:33,796 --> 01:41:35,756
Aaaaahhhhhh!

1797
01:41:35,839 --> 01:41:37,841
- Oh!
- Aaahhh!

1798
01:41:38,968 --> 01:41:43,013
( Screaming and shouting )

1799
01:41:43,097 --> 01:41:46,892
( Ollie screaming )

1800
01:41:49,728 --> 01:41:50,771
AMANDA: Ohh!

1801
01:41:50,854 --> 01:41:53,232
Aaah! Aaaahhhh!

1802
01:41:55,651 --> 01:41:57,695
Aaah! Aaaaahhhhh!

1803
01:42:11,417 --> 01:42:12,751
IRENE: All that screaming!

1804
01:42:13,919 --> 01:42:16,171
DAN:Are they out there?
Can they see us?

1805
01:42:16,255 --> 01:42:18,924
( Honks car horn )

1806
01:42:26,098 --> 01:42:28,517
Let me-- let me in!
Let me in!

1807
01:42:28,601 --> 01:42:32,563
( Screaming )

1808
01:42:36,984 --> 01:42:38,444
( Screams die )

1809
01:42:42,948 --> 01:42:44,450
Are we going?

1810
01:42:51,290 --> 01:42:52,541
- No.
- Yeah.

1811
01:42:52,625 --> 01:42:54,710
- No! No!
- Yeah!

1812
01:42:54,793 --> 01:42:56,086
- Daddy.
- David.

1813
01:42:56,170 --> 01:42:58,088
- David, no.
- Daddy, no.

1814
01:42:58,172 --> 01:42:59,923
- David!
- Daddy!

1815
01:43:00,007 --> 01:43:01,508
Get back in the car!

1816
01:43:01,592 --> 01:43:03,218
- Daddy!
- David!

1817
01:43:03,302 --> 01:43:04,720
( Screaming )

1818
01:43:04,803 --> 01:43:06,889
( Monster shrieking )

1819
01:43:13,604 --> 01:43:15,230
Oh, my God!

1820
01:43:15,314 --> 01:43:16,649
Aaahhh!

1821
01:43:16,732 --> 01:43:18,067
( Shrieking )

1822
01:43:18,150 --> 01:43:20,110
AMANDA: Oh, my God!

1823
01:43:40,214 --> 01:43:41,256
We gotta go.

1824
01:43:44,093 --> 01:43:45,177
( Engine starts )

1825
01:45:31,241 --> 01:45:33,076
( Distant monster roars )

1826
01:45:37,915 --> 01:45:40,375
( Distant monster roars )

1827
01:45:40,459 --> 01:45:42,461
DAVID: I told her I'd fix it.

1828
01:45:45,839 --> 01:45:49,176
Front window... broken open.

1829
01:45:52,930 --> 01:45:54,097
Tree.

1830
01:45:56,225 --> 01:45:59,645
My... grandfather's tree.

1831
01:46:06,276 --> 01:46:10,030
( Distant monster roars )

1832
01:46:14,701 --> 01:46:18,038
I'm sorry, David,
I'm just so sorry.

1833
01:46:33,095 --> 01:46:37,641
DAVID: Let's, uh... see how far this...

1834
01:46:39,393 --> 01:46:41,645
fuel takes us, huh?

1835
01:46:41,728 --> 01:46:44,648
( Engine humming )

1836
01:46:44,731 --> 01:46:46,733
Maybe we'll get clear of the mist.

1837
01:47:50,756 --> 01:47:52,257
( Giant, heavy footsteps )

1838
01:47:59,514 --> 01:48:01,016
( Giant, heavy footsteps )

1839
01:48:10,859 --> 01:48:13,362
( Massive bellow )

1840
01:48:29,878 --> 01:48:32,381
( Bellows )

1841
01:48:41,390 --> 01:48:44,059
( Bellows )

1842
01:49:15,841 --> 01:49:18,343
( Engine faltering )

1843
01:49:25,100 --> 01:49:28,061
( Engine faltering )

1844
01:49:39,948 --> 01:49:41,491
( Engine dies )

1845
01:50:03,013 --> 01:50:04,264
DAN: Well...

1846
01:50:05,515 --> 01:50:07,476
we gave it a good shot.

1847
01:50:08,894 --> 01:50:10,395
Nobody can say we didn't.

1848
01:50:12,397 --> 01:50:14,149
Nope.

1849
01:50:14,232 --> 01:50:16,026
Nobody can say that.

1850
01:50:20,906 --> 01:50:23,575
( Distant monsters roar )

1851
01:50:46,807 --> 01:50:49,434
( Distant monsters roar )

1852
01:51:06,076 --> 01:51:07,577
( Sighs )

1853
01:51:45,031 --> 01:51:46,283
Well...

1854
01:51:48,285 --> 01:51:49,828
We got, uh...

1855
01:51:54,207 --> 01:51:55,458
four.

1856
01:51:59,754 --> 01:52:01,006
Four bullets.

1857
01:52:05,552 --> 01:52:07,053
But there's five of us.

1858
01:52:17,606 --> 01:52:19,357
I'll figure something out.

1859
01:52:21,818 --> 01:52:23,278
( Bullet drops into chamber )

1860
01:52:29,367 --> 01:52:32,454
( Distant monsters roar )

1861
01:53:03,276 --> 01:53:05,779
( Distant monsters roar )

1862
01:53:17,582 --> 01:53:19,918
( Gunshots )

1863
01:53:27,259 --> 01:53:29,928
DAVID: Aaaaahhhhh!

1864
01:53:31,012 --> 01:53:32,264
Aaahhh!

1865
01:53:34,933 --> 01:53:37,686
( Weeping loudly )

1866
01:53:56,746 --> 01:54:00,500
( Dry firing )

1867
01:54:10,885 --> 01:54:13,680
Aah! Aah!

1868
01:54:18,143 --> 01:54:19,561
Come on!

1869
01:54:25,567 --> 01:54:26,901
Come on!

1870
01:54:28,194 --> 01:54:29,696
Come on!

1871
01:54:33,074 --> 01:54:36,077
( Softly ) Come on. Come on.

1872
01:54:36,161 --> 01:54:39,331
- Come on.
- ( distant bellow )

1873
01:54:46,588 --> 01:54:47,881
Come on.

1874
01:54:48,089 --> 01:54:49,674
Come on.

1875
01:54:49,924 --> 01:54:51,468
Come on.

1876
01:54:52,510 --> 01:54:54,637
Come on, come <i>on!</i>

1877
01:54:54,846 --> 01:54:57,557
Come on! Come on!

1878
01:54:57,640 --> 01:55:00,101
( Distant monsters roar )

1879
01:55:00,185 --> 01:55:03,938
( low rumble rising )

1880
01:55:04,022 --> 01:55:06,691
( Massive bellow )

1881
01:56:16,261 --> 01:56:19,055
( Helicopter passes overhead )

1882
01:56:34,696 --> 01:56:37,157
They're-- they're dead.

1883
01:56:37,240 --> 01:56:38,741
For what?

1884
01:56:41,244 --> 01:56:43,329
( Crying )

1885
01:56:43,413 --> 01:56:45,373
Aah!

1886
01:56:45,457 --> 01:56:48,042
Aaaaahhhhhh!

1887
01:56:49,752 --> 01:56:52,922
( Screaming )

1888
02:01:07,885 --> 02:01:10,388
<i>( Helicopter rotors whirr)</i>

1889
02:01:21,399 --> 02:01:23,901
<i>( Ground vehicle passes)</i>

1890
02:01:42,253 --> 02:01:44,756
<i>( Distant helicopter approaches)</i>

1891
02:02:18,915 --> 02:02:21,417
<i>( Ground vehicle passes)</i>

1892
02:02:35,264 --> 02:02:37,767
<i>( Distant helicopter approaches)</i>

1893
02:03:05,211 --> 02:03:07,713
<i>( Ground vehicle passes)</i>

1894
02:03:29,735 --> 02:03:32,238
<i>( Ground vehicle passes)</i>

1895
02:03:53,259 --> 02:03:55,761
<i>( Distant helicopter approaches)</i>

1896
02:04:34,258 --> 02:04:36,928
<i>( Distant helicopter approaches)</i>

1897
02:04:53,361 --> 02:04:55,863
<i>( Ground vehicle passes)</i>

1898
